1
00:00:34,959 --> 00:00:38,519
(Music: "It Takes A Lot To
Know A Man"" by Damien Rice)

2
00:00:40,959 --> 00:00:43,479
"What are you so afraid to lose?"

3
00:00:45,319 --> 00:00:49,559
"What is it you're thinking
that will happen if you do?"

4
00:00:52,239 --> 00:00:55,319
"What are you so afraid to lose?"

5
00:00:58,999 --> 00:01:02,639
"What is it you're thinking
that will happen if you do?"

6
00:01:04,999 --> 00:01:08,399
"What are you so afraid to lose?"

7
00:01:10,839 --> 00:01:13,359
(The music fades.)

8
00:01:19,879 --> 00:01:23,159
I still need a signature,
Mr. Albrecht. Here.

9
00:01:25,279 --> 00:01:28,479
Take care out there.
Goodbye forever!

10
00:01:29,559 --> 00:01:31,519
Yeah, fuck you too.

11
00:01:34,119 --> 00:01:36,479
(Somber music)

12
00:01:50,119 --> 00:01:52,079
Mr. Albrecht?

13
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:54,399
Jörg Albrecht?
- Ms. Bittner?

14
00:01:54,559 --> 00:01:58,239
We had talked on the phone.
Go ahead, get in.

15
00:01:58,439 --> 00:02:00,999
You can put your
bag on the back seat.

16
00:02:01,159 --> 00:02:03,119
Thank you.

17
00:02:05,719 --> 00:02:07,919
(The engine is started.)

18
00:02:12,159 --> 00:02:14,479
(Soft, tense music)

19
00:02:23,599 --> 00:02:25,559
Can I smoke?

20
00:02:26,519 --> 00:02:28,479
Please not in the car.

21
00:02:31,839 --> 00:02:34,399
You can drop me off
in the Leonhard district.

22
00:02:34,559 --> 00:02:36,519
At the Eros Center, please.

23
00:02:38,559 --> 00:02:40,519
So I'll show you your apartment.

24
00:02:40,679 --> 00:02:44,079
From there, you can then
attend to your own needs.

25
00:02:50,519 --> 00:02:53,239
(Dark, atmospheric music)

26
00:02:55,799 --> 00:02:58,199
Here, in this building?
- Yes.

27
00:03:37,159 --> 00:03:39,479
(Soft, tense music)

28
00:03:47,599 --> 00:03:49,639
I know where I know you from.

29
00:03:55,239 --> 00:03:57,359
From the trial.

30
00:04:05,399 --> 00:04:07,559
What are you doing here?

31
00:04:12,359 --> 00:04:14,399
(She breathes heavily.)

32
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:17,119
(Dark music)

33
00:04:22,759 --> 00:04:24,879
(Crows cawing)

34
00:04:25,399 --> 00:04:27,359
(Harsh, eerie music)

35
00:05:04,799 --> 00:05:06,759
I am a doctor.

36
00:05:07,639 --> 00:05:11,239
But being a doctor also
means I know anatomy very well.

37
00:05:11,639 --> 00:05:14,119
With nerve points,
with pain.

38
00:05:14,279 --> 00:05:16,239
The thing is simple:

39
00:05:16,559 --> 00:05:19,239
Tell me who the other one was.
The name.

40
00:05:19,639 --> 00:05:21,599
The name!
- The name.

41
00:05:21,759 --> 00:05:24,319
Please tell us the name.
Tell us!

42
00:05:24,479 --> 00:05:26,759
Help! Help!

43
00:05:27,079 --> 00:05:29,039
Help!

44
00:05:29,759 --> 00:05:31,919
(distantly:) Help!

45
00:05:33,919 --> 00:05:36,079
What's the other one's name?
- Fuck you!

46
00:05:38,039 --> 00:05:40,319
(Ominous music)

47
00:05:52,319 --> 00:05:54,279
(quietly:) The name!

48
00:05:54,439 --> 00:05:56,679
They'll kill me
if I say it.

49
00:05:57,679 --> 00:06:00,079
(Heavy breathing.)

50
00:06:01,679 --> 00:06:04,239
What's the other one's name?
- He'll kill me!

51
00:06:05,999 --> 00:06:08,359
He'll kill me,
don't you get it?

52
00:06:14,079 --> 00:06:16,359
(Eerie music)

53
00:06:19,239 --> 00:06:21,799
What is that?
- You don't need to be afraid.

54
00:06:21,959 --> 00:06:23,919
What is that?

55
00:06:24,079 --> 00:06:26,759
You'll tell us the name ...
the name!

56
00:06:26,919 --> 00:06:29,759
What is that, what's in the syringe?
- The name!

57
00:06:29,919 --> 00:06:31,879
It's not that simple!

58
00:06:32,279 --> 00:06:34,239
What's in it?
- The name!

59
00:06:34,399 --> 00:06:36,719
(Man:) We're seeing this through.
- The name!

60
00:06:36,879 --> 00:06:39,279
The name, the name!
- He'll kill me!

61
00:06:39,559 --> 00:06:41,679
The name!
- What's in it?

62
00:06:41,839 --> 00:06:44,079
The name!
- What's in the syringe?

63
00:06:44,239 --> 00:06:46,199
The name!

64
00:06:46,399 --> 00:06:48,879
(shouting:) The name,
the name, the name!

65
00:06:49,039 --> 00:06:51,199
(whispering:) Stefan
Freund. Stefan Freund.

66
00:06:53,919 --> 00:06:55,879
Stefan Freund.

67
00:06:56,279 --> 00:07:00,319
But you didn't hear it from me, okay?
You didn't hear it from me!

68
00:07:00,479 --> 00:07:02,439
We'll check that.

69
00:07:02,599 --> 00:07:06,319
We'll check that, and
if you lied, we'll kill you.

70
00:07:06,479 --> 00:07:08,439
I didn't lie!

71
00:07:08,599 --> 00:07:11,399
Freund was back then with
the Devils in Reuttlingen.

72
00:07:11,559 --> 00:07:13,719
Please, I've already paid for it!

73
00:07:14,639 --> 00:07:16,759
I've already paid!

74
00:07:17,239 --> 00:07:20,919
(schreit:) Ouch, stop it! Stop it!

75
00:07:21,079 --> 00:07:23,199
I'm not like that anymore!

76
00:07:23,679 --> 00:07:26,679
Please! Please ...

77
00:07:27,479 --> 00:07:29,439
(He sobs.)

78
00:07:29,639 --> 00:07:31,759
Mareike wanted to live, too.

79
00:07:33,359 --> 00:07:35,479
I'm not like that anymore!

80
00:07:36,239 --> 00:07:38,199
Stop it!

81
00:07:40,719 --> 00:07:43,079
(Shrill, eerie music)

82
00:07:43,959 --> 00:07:45,919
(Sobbing)

83
00:08:11,959 --> 00:08:14,079
(Kettle whistles.)

84
00:08:14,399 --> 00:08:16,399
(Pop music from the radio)

85
00:08:28,279 --> 00:08:30,439
(Rhythmic pop music)

86
00:08:50,639 --> 00:08:52,639
Dad?
- Hm?

87
00:08:52,799 --> 00:08:55,039
Sabine's having her
birthday this weekend.

88
00:08:55,199 --> 00:08:58,599
I need to take a break.
- At her parents' weekend house.

89
00:08:58,759 --> 00:09:00,719
And everyone's staying over.

90
00:09:00,879 --> 00:09:02,879
I need a sleeping bag, too.

91
00:09:03,039 --> 00:09:05,239
What does that mean?
I haven't said yes yet.

92
00:09:05,399 --> 00:09:07,759
Please! I'm not a
little girl anymore!

93
00:09:07,919 --> 00:09:09,879
That's the whole point.

94
00:09:10,039 --> 00:09:12,759
Do you know how embarrassing that is,
when I have to say,

95
00:09:12,919 --> 00:09:14,879
that I'm not allowed to come along?

96
00:09:15,039 --> 00:09:17,239
Did Sabine only
invite girls?

97
00:09:18,839 --> 00:09:21,839
I don't know. Yeah ... no?

98
00:09:21,999 --> 00:09:25,079
What now?
- Yeah, there are boys there too.

99
00:09:25,799 --> 00:09:27,759
And Leon.

100
00:09:27,919 --> 00:09:30,439
Leon? How old is he?
- 14.

101
00:09:30,599 --> 00:09:32,639
147

102
00:09:33,759 --> 00:09:36,079
I'd like to get to
know him first.

103
00:09:36,239 --> 00:09:38,319
The party is today!
No way!

104
00:09:38,479 --> 00:09:41,279
You just have to make it work somehow.
I don't know how either.

105
00:09:41,439 --> 00:09:43,759
I'll ask Mom.
- She's not back until tomorrow.

106
00:09:43,919 --> 00:09:45,919
Then I'm just going
without your permission.

107
00:09:46,079 --> 00:09:48,039
You will not!

108
00:09:48,239 --> 00:09:50,399
You will not,
you mustn't!

109
00:09:50,559 --> 00:09:52,519
Come!

110
00:09:54,399 --> 00:09:56,719
(Rhythmic pop music)

111
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:29,039
(Cell phone rings.)

112
00:10:29,319 --> 00:10:31,759
Good morning, Sebastian.
- "Morning, Thorsten."

113
00:10:31,919 --> 00:10:34,799
"Made it through the night shift?"
- I could rip trees out of the ground.

114
00:10:34,959 --> 00:10:36,959
"Very good. We have a client."

115
00:10:37,119 --> 00:10:40,039
"Kluge, corner of Rothenwaldstraße."
- Which number?

116
00:10:40,199 --> 00:10:42,279
"You'll see. See you in a bit."

117
00:10:46,839 --> 00:10:49,759
The guy is called Abdella al-Hamadı,
the other one Michael ...

118
00:10:49,919 --> 00:10:51,879
Morning!
- Morning.

119
00:10:52,039 --> 00:10:54,399
Morning, gentlemen.
- Morning, Dr. Vogt.

120
00:10:55,279 --> 00:10:57,999
So, you're doing
the photos first? Okay.

121
00:10:58,679 --> 00:11:00,639
In here?
- Yes, in there.

122
00:11:00,799 --> 00:11:04,799
The garbage man Abdella al-Hamadi
found him, bin number six.

123
00:11:05,359 --> 00:11:08,279
Was he already dead?
- Yes, he was already dead.

124
00:11:08,439 --> 00:11:10,399
Rigor mortis is in the jaw, neck

125
00:11:10,559 --> 00:11:12,839
and in the upper
extremities to be detected.

126
00:11:12,999 --> 00:11:16,079
So, the time of
death was last night?

127
00:11:16,279 --> 00:11:18,599
Yes, about ten to
twelve hours ago.

128
00:11:18,999 --> 00:11:21,479
"One morning you
no longer wake up."

129
00:11:21,999 --> 00:11:24,239
"The birds sing, as
they always sang."

130
00:11:24,399 --> 00:11:27,639
"Nothing changes this course
of the day, only you have gone."

131
00:11:27,799 --> 00:11:31,799
Goethe. I can only tell you
more about the cause of death later.

132
00:11:31,959 --> 00:11:34,959
Did anyone see that
this garbage man - what's his name?

133
00:11:35,119 --> 00:11:37,279
Abdella al-Hamadi.
- ... had found him?

134
00:11:37,439 --> 00:11:40,719
Yes, his colleague, Michael Petro.
He saw it.

135
00:11:42,399 --> 00:11:46,159
What's interesting: This is
Jörg Albrecht.

136
00:11:46,359 --> 00:11:48,319
He had papers on him.

137
00:11:48,479 --> 00:11:50,919
Was released from JVA Stammheim
yesterday.

138
00:11:51,079 --> 00:11:53,039
What was he in for?

139
00:11:54,599 --> 00:11:56,799
Rape resulting in death.

140
00:11:59,879 --> 00:12:02,319
(Soft, dark music)

141
00:12:19,079 --> 00:12:21,359
The footage here
is so distorted,

142
00:12:21,519 --> 00:12:25,079
that the perpetrator, who had kidnapped
and abused the girl,

143
00:12:25,239 --> 00:12:27,199
could not be identified.

144
00:12:27,359 --> 00:12:29,319
So the perpetrator thought.

145
00:12:29,479 --> 00:12:31,639
But the colleagues at the LKA
managed to

146
00:12:31,799 --> 00:12:34,759
digitally reverse this alteration

147
00:12:35,839 --> 00:12:37,839
Albrecht.
- Yes.

148
00:12:38,879 --> 00:12:42,519
He came from a broken home,
was himself a victim of abuse

149
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:46,279
and, um, was noticed as a teenager
for animal cruelty.

150
00:12:46,439 --> 00:12:48,399
What exactly?
- Small animals.

151
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:52,399
Then he seriously injured a mare
with a knife. Youth prison.

152
00:12:52,599 --> 00:12:54,799
That's when he met his new
friends.

153
00:12:54,959 --> 00:12:56,919
With the Devils.

154
00:12:57,079 --> 00:12:59,399
'A motorcycle club,
there isn't one anymore.

155
00:13:00,719 --> 00:13:03,039
(Soft, eerie music)

156
00:13:19,959 --> 00:13:21,919
(Doorbell)

157
00:13:27,439 --> 00:13:29,399
(doorbell)

158
00:13:30,119 --> 00:13:32,399
Hello!
- Hello.

159
00:13:33,279 --> 00:13:37,439
A package for Mr. Freund?
- But it's to be handed over in person.

160
00:13:38,679 --> 00:13:42,439
He won't be back until this evening.
Retraining.

161
00:13:43,799 --> 00:13:47,519
Where's the retraining?
- At ... at ... Henneling.

162
00:13:47,839 --> 00:13:50,399
That's the automotive
supplier in Obertürkheim?

163
00:13:50,559 --> 00:13:53,719
Yes ... Yes, exactly.
Shall I take the package?

164
00:13:53,879 --> 00:13:56,839
No, no.
- We'll take it with us.

165
00:13:56,999 --> 00:13:59,199
Thank you.
- You're welcome.

166
00:14:04,759 --> 00:14:07,639
And in the end, he killed her.
- Yes.

167
00:14:08,559 --> 00:14:12,439
She was kidnapped, for 72
hours abused and then strangled.

168
00:14:12,599 --> 00:14:14,559
Her name was Mareike Menadt.

169
00:14:14,719 --> 00:14:16,719
How old was she?
- 16.

170
00:14:16,919 --> 00:14:18,999
Jörg Albrecht got 15 years.

171
00:14:19,159 --> 00:14:23,079
In prison, he participated in
a re- socialization program.

172
00:14:23,359 --> 00:14:26,159
He had good behavior, a
favorable social prognosis.

173
00:14:26,319 --> 00:14:29,119
Why did he serve his sentence
in full?

174
00:14:29,279 --> 00:14:31,439
Because there was a
second person in the room.

175
00:14:31,599 --> 00:14:33,759
The one who filmed everything.

176
00:14:34,319 --> 00:14:37,599
The one whose name Jörg
Albrecht didn't want to reveal.

177
00:14:37,839 --> 00:14:40,559
The one who might also have
committed Mareike's murder.

178
00:14:40,719 --> 00:14:43,679
That's why they didn't grant him
early release despite his good behavior.

179
00:14:43,839 --> 00:14:45,799
Can I just interrupt?
- Mhm.

180
00:14:45,959 --> 00:14:49,799
Ms. Bittner is waiting in the office.
Jörg Albrecht's probation officer.

181
00:14:51,119 --> 00:14:53,679
We were scheduled at exactly nine
to meet at the prison.

182
00:14:53,839 --> 00:14:56,359
I was late,
he was no longer there.

183
00:14:56,759 --> 00:15:00,599
The gatekeeper told me that he
got into a car with a woman.

184
00:15:00,759 --> 00:15:02,759
At nine.
But he doesn't answer his phone.

185
00:15:02,919 --> 00:15:05,279
That's when you
reported it to the police.

186
00:15:05,439 --> 00:15:07,559
No, but when I was
about to leave yesterday,

187
00:15:07,719 --> 00:15:09,919
my car had
a punctured tire.

188
00:15:10,079 --> 00:15:12,239
I only noticed it
after a kilometer.

189
00:15:12,479 --> 00:15:14,719
What's the gatekeeper's name?
- Mr. Engel.

190
00:15:15,519 --> 00:15:18,199
The girl's relatives?
- Her parents.

191
00:15:18,519 --> 00:15:20,559
Simone and Frank Menadt.

192
00:15:21,039 --> 00:15:24,079
He's a doctor, and they are also
the private prosecutors.

193
00:15:24,719 --> 00:15:28,599
Mareike Mendt was her only child.
No aunts, no uncles.

194
00:15:29,199 --> 00:15:32,879
Could they have known that Jörg
Albrecht was being released yesterday?

195
00:15:33,039 --> 00:15:36,119
Co-prosecutors are informed
of the date of release.

196
00:15:36,279 --> 00:15:38,239
Mhm.

197
00:15:38,399 --> 00:15:40,359
What's the address?
- Sorry?

198
00:15:40,519 --> 00:15:44,359
The address.
- Uh ... Im Schöttinger 4.

199
00:15:44,679 --> 00:15:46,639
Thank you.

200
00:15:48,199 --> 00:15:50,599
(Bird cawing)

201
00:15:53,839 --> 00:15:57,239
(Music: "It Takes A Lot To
Know A Man"" by Damien Rice)

202
00:16:00,519 --> 00:16:03,999
"What are you so afraid to lose?"

203
00:16:07,439 --> 00:16:11,719
"What is it you're thinking
that will happen if you do?"

204
00:16:13,359 --> 00:16:16,679
"What are you so afraid to lose?"

205
00:16:19,959 --> 00:16:23,959
"What is it you're thinking
that will happen if you do?"

206
00:16:26,519 --> 00:16:29,959
"What are you so afraid to lose?"

207
00:16:32,599 --> 00:16:36,639
"What is it you're thinking
that will happen if you do?"

208
00:16:51,759 --> 00:16:53,719
(Doorbell)

209
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:15,359
Bootz, Criminal Police, Stuttgart.
This is my colleague Lannert.

210
00:17:16,159 --> 00:17:18,639
Are you Mr. and Mrs. Mendt?
- Yes.

211
00:17:20,079 --> 00:17:22,479
Jörg Albrecht has been murdered.

212
00:17:23,439 --> 00:17:25,599
I can't believe we'd live to see this!

213
00:17:26,999 --> 00:17:29,559
May we come in for a moment?
- Of course.

214
00:17:30,159 --> 00:17:32,119
Come this way.
Here, straight ahead.

215
00:17:32,279 --> 00:17:34,639
My wife will show you to the living room.

216
00:17:38,119 --> 00:17:40,079
Please.

217
00:17:40,799 --> 00:17:43,279
(Soft, dark music)

218
00:17:46,959 --> 00:17:49,319
Please excuse
my wife's remarks.

219
00:17:49,559 --> 00:17:52,159
But it is a relief for us
to know,

220
00:17:52,319 --> 00:17:55,439
that Mr. Albrecht is dead.
How did it happen, who did it?

221
00:17:55,679 --> 00:17:58,639
We don't know.
He was found this morning.

222
00:17:58,839 --> 00:18:02,079
You were both here yesterday morning?
- You're suspecting us?

223
00:18:02,879 --> 00:18:05,559
You knew
when Jörg Albrecht would be released.

224
00:18:05,719 --> 00:18:07,679
That's right.

225
00:18:09,359 --> 00:18:11,319
We were here.

226
00:18:11,479 --> 00:18:13,879
You vouch for each other,
I assume?

227
00:18:14,039 --> 00:18:17,359
Yes.
- We have to ask you that.

228
00:18:17,519 --> 00:18:20,519
What would you have done
against Mr. Albrecht?

229
00:18:20,799 --> 00:18:22,759
What do you mean?

230
00:18:22,919 --> 00:18:26,839
He was the only one who knew
who else was involved. And did nothing.

231
00:18:27,479 --> 00:18:29,519
Probably nothing.

232
00:18:29,679 --> 00:18:32,559
Despite a 15-year prison sentence,
he didn't betray him.

233
00:18:32,719 --> 00:18:35,479
Today he probably wouldn't
have done it either.

234
00:18:35,639 --> 00:18:37,599
He didn't betray him,

235
00:18:37,759 --> 00:18:40,879
because the detectives back then
weren't persistent enough.

236
00:18:41,039 --> 00:18:43,119
They should have kept asking longer.

237
00:18:43,759 --> 00:18:45,959
We had lost Mareike.

238
00:18:47,319 --> 00:18:49,639
The authorities back then, the ...

239
00:18:52,039 --> 00:18:53,999
We even had to tell them,

240
00:18:54,159 --> 00:18:56,639
that there must have been
a second man.

241
00:18:57,079 --> 00:18:59,519
How did you know that?
- From the film.

242
00:19:00,519 --> 00:19:03,159
Do you have a film?
Can we see it?

243
00:19:08,519 --> 00:19:10,479
Simone, I can't.

244
00:19:12,239 --> 00:19:14,199
Yes ... Yes, fine, then ...

245
00:19:15,479 --> 00:19:17,719
Come, I'll show you.

246
00:19:19,439 --> 00:19:21,999
(Soft, atmospheric music)

247
00:19:37,679 --> 00:19:39,639
Where did you get those?

248
00:19:39,799 --> 00:19:41,759
They're circulating online.

249
00:19:43,319 --> 00:19:45,279
They tortured my daughter...

250
00:19:46,279 --> 00:19:49,359
... for three days and nights
straight.

251
00:19:52,719 --> 00:19:56,079
Yes, maybe, uh, could you
uh, take a look at the pictures?

252
00:19:56,879 --> 00:19:59,879
We already know the photos.
- Oh, you know the photos?

253
00:20:00,039 --> 00:20:03,439
Take another look, maybe
it will help you with the work.

254
00:20:03,599 --> 00:20:05,959
We already took a good look
at you.

255
00:20:06,119 --> 00:20:08,599
We would be interested in
this film.

256
00:20:10,319 --> 00:20:14,079
They tortured my daughter
for three days and nights.

257
00:20:14,279 --> 00:20:16,719
Yes.
- Just take another look.

258
00:20:16,879 --> 00:20:18,839
They abused her.

259
00:20:19,359 --> 00:20:21,319
And I wasn't there for her.

260
00:20:22,559 --> 00:20:26,039
She must have wondered why
her father and I weren't there.

261
00:20:26,199 --> 00:20:28,159
Why we weren't helping her!

262
00:20:29,159 --> 00:20:31,399
And then they killed her!

263
00:20:32,039 --> 00:20:34,759
I wish I could have endured that
for her.

264
00:20:34,919 --> 00:20:36,959
And then they ...

265
00:20:37,879 --> 00:20:41,479
... those animals put the
photos up online, sold them.

266
00:20:41,759 --> 00:20:44,639
Strangers took pleasure
in these images.

267
00:20:44,919 --> 00:20:47,519
Wasn't that stopped?
- Yes, of course.

268
00:20:47,679 --> 00:20:51,079
Of course, they've tried that. They've
had the content blocked again and again ...

269
00:20:51,279 --> 00:20:54,439
... Over and over, it gets blocked.
But the internet never forgets.

270
00:20:54,759 --> 00:20:58,999
And eventually there's another one
of those ... One of those providers in ...

271
00:20:59,719 --> 00:21:01,679
... Russia or in Togo.

272
00:21:01,999 --> 00:21:06,319
And eventually the ones who
bought the pictures re-upload them.

273
00:21:08,359 --> 00:21:10,999
To ... Yes, to trade them.

274
00:21:12,559 --> 00:21:14,519
For other photos.

275
00:21:15,039 --> 00:21:17,799
Like pirated copies, that's
how the police explained it to us.

276
00:21:17,959 --> 00:21:20,359
She also said she was
powerless against it.

277
00:21:20,639 --> 00:21:23,279
And, um ... this film?

278
00:21:25,119 --> 00:21:27,679
Ms. Mendt, can
we take a look at it?

279
00:21:27,959 --> 00:21:30,399
Can you please take
your hands off it?

280
00:21:30,559 --> 00:21:32,519
Please?

281
00:21:32,679 --> 00:21:34,679
Don't touch my computer!

282
00:21:34,839 --> 00:21:37,359
You wanted to show us this film.
- Wait!

283
00:21:44,199 --> 00:21:46,159
Here ...

284
00:21:46,679 --> 00:21:49,879
At second 35 ...
the image moves.

285
00:22:08,519 --> 00:22:10,879
They didn't just kill Mareike.

286
00:22:12,119 --> 00:22:14,079
They destroyed three lives.

287
00:22:18,519 --> 00:22:20,919
(Soft music)

288
00:22:27,039 --> 00:22:29,239
That's when the camera moved.

289
00:22:40,279 --> 00:22:43,999
Thank you for your time and the infor-
mation about the online businesses.

290
00:22:44,159 --> 00:22:46,159
You are the first.
- The first what?

291
00:22:46,319 --> 00:22:49,759
Since the trial. The murderer
was reported on constantly.

292
00:22:49,919 --> 00:22:53,439
But the last reporter only wanted
to photograph Mareike's room.

293
00:22:53,599 --> 00:22:55,559
And stole photos.
- Yes?

294
00:22:55,759 --> 00:22:57,799
That was 15 years ago ...
_ "Vogt_"

295
00:22:57,999 --> 00:23:01,439
We haven't yet finished
Mr. Albrecht's autopsy.

296
00:23:01,599 --> 00:23:04,039
But I can say two things
with certainty.

297
00:23:04,199 --> 00:23:08,199
Someone gave him an
IV in the elbow crease.

298
00:23:08,439 --> 00:23:11,359
"And he died of an
overdose of pentobarbital."

299
00:23:11,519 --> 00:23:14,039
" Veterinarians use that
to put them to sleep, right?

300
00:23:14,439 --> 00:23:17,719
It used to be a sedative.
Not everyone woke back up.

301
00:23:17,999 --> 00:23:22,039
Who can easily get their hands on it?
- Anyone with manufacturer access.

302
00:23:22,519 --> 00:23:25,879
"Pharmacists, maybe.
Veterinarians for sure."

303
00:23:26,039 --> 00:23:27,999
Doctors?
- Yes, too.

304
00:23:29,479 --> 00:23:32,239
Okay. Understood.
Thank you, Mr. Vogt.

305
00:23:35,599 --> 00:23:37,559
(Doorbell)

306
00:23:39,879 --> 00:23:42,159
Mr. Mendt,
you practiced as a doctor?

307
00:23:42,359 --> 00:23:44,599
Yes.
- I'm placing you under temporary custody.

308
00:23:45,319 --> 00:23:47,919
On suspicion of murder
of Jörg Albrecht.

309
00:23:48,079 --> 00:23:50,999
He was killed with a lethal
dose of pentobarbital.

310
00:23:51,159 --> 00:23:54,759
Ah. May I get my coat?
- Go ahead.

311
00:23:58,679 --> 00:24:00,959
(Quiet, atmospheric music)

312
00:24:02,719 --> 00:24:04,679
We'll be right back.

313
00:24:17,519 --> 00:24:19,479
(She sighs.)

314
00:24:25,479 --> 00:24:27,439
Do you have children?

315
00:24:29,279 --> 00:24:31,239
Not anymore.

316
00:24:31,439 --> 00:24:33,399
And you?

317
00:24:33,639 --> 00:24:37,159
You think I can't fathom
what's going on inside you.

318
00:24:37,399 --> 00:24:40,199
But I have a daughter, too.
She asked me

319
00:24:40,359 --> 00:24:43,119
if she could go to her first
sleepover.

320
00:24:43,279 --> 00:24:45,519
When can I contact my
lawyer?

321
00:24:45,679 --> 00:24:47,719
In the President's office.

322
00:24:52,159 --> 00:24:55,999
Does Claudia Bittner mean anything to you?
- No. Did she kill Albrecht?

323
00:24:58,519 --> 00:25:00,479
I understand.

324
00:25:00,839 --> 00:25:04,919
There is no greater pain
than the loss of a child.

325
00:25:05,079 --> 00:25:08,719
If one tries to imagine
an increa- se in the pain,

326
00:25:08,879 --> 00:25:12,239
one thinks it would be so great,
that it should kill you instantly.

327
00:25:12,399 --> 00:25:14,359
Unbearable.

328
00:25:14,959 --> 00:25:18,199
But then the pain comes,
and you endure it.

329
00:25:18,879 --> 00:25:21,479
And it comes from the certainty
that the man

330
00:25:21,679 --> 00:25:24,999
who tore Mareike out of this life,
who destroyed everything

331
00:25:25,159 --> 00:25:27,159
that Mareike could have become,

332
00:25:27,319 --> 00:25:30,079
that this man, after prison,
gets something

333
00:25:30,359 --> 00:25:34,079
that is denied to you and your daughter
: a fresh start.

334
00:25:34,479 --> 00:25:36,879
A new life,
a new chance.

335
00:25:37,639 --> 00:25:40,199
And that is unbearable.

336
00:25:40,639 --> 00:25:43,399
That has tormented you and your wife.
- Yes, it has.

337
00:25:43,559 --> 00:25:45,559
To put it bluntly,

338
00:25:45,759 --> 00:25:49,079
The justice system, the media - everyone
cared about Albrecht.

339
00:25:49,839 --> 00:25:53,279
For his placement,
his psychological assessment,

340
00:25:53,479 --> 00:25:55,519
his social prognosis.

341
00:25:55,959 --> 00:25:58,239
He underwent
psychiatric sessions

342
00:25:58,399 --> 00:26:00,359
and was able to work through everything.

343
00:26:00,839 --> 00:26:02,879
But both of you
were left on your own.

344
00:26:03,039 --> 00:26:06,079
It was made clear to you that
society didn't care,

345
00:26:06,239 --> 00:26:08,399
how you coped with
your loss.

346
00:26:08,839 --> 00:26:10,879
Yes.

347
00:26:12,519 --> 00:26:15,039
Are you a supporter
of the death penalty?

348
00:26:17,039 --> 00:26:20,039
There is a common correlation
between education level

349
00:26:20,199 --> 00:26:22,159
and attitude toward it.

350
00:26:22,319 --> 00:26:24,919
The less educated,
the greater the support.

351
00:26:28,239 --> 00:26:30,559
The mobile carrier's
analysis.

352
00:26:30,719 --> 00:26:34,199
Both phones have been
unused and static for two days.

353
00:26:34,359 --> 00:26:36,679
When is your lawyer coming?
- Probably stuck in traffic.

354
00:26:36,839 --> 00:26:40,199
The surveillance camera in front of the prison
doesn't help us either.

355
00:26:40,359 --> 00:26:42,559
Why?
- You only see a car pull up

356
00:26:42,719 --> 00:26:45,599
and Jörg Albrecht get in.
- The license plate?

357
00:26:46,919 --> 00:26:49,079
It's been obscured.
- Thanks.

358
00:26:50,719 --> 00:26:52,679
Yes ...

359
00:26:55,319 --> 00:26:57,279
I'll take it from here.

360
00:27:00,359 --> 00:27:02,839
You knew
when Jörg Albrecht would be released.

361
00:27:02,999 --> 00:27:05,959
You slashed the tires of his
probation officer

362
00:27:06,119 --> 00:27:08,159
and kidnapped him.
- No.

363
00:27:08,639 --> 00:27:10,599
I don't even know her!

364
00:27:10,959 --> 00:27:13,759
I believe that to this day
you still suffer greatly

365
00:27:13,919 --> 00:27:17,359
from having lost your daughter.
You have my full understanding.

366
00:27:17,519 --> 00:27:20,559
But your suffering does not elevate
you above the law.

367
00:27:23,039 --> 00:27:25,719
As an uninvolved party,
that's a very simple perspective.

368
00:27:25,879 --> 00:27:28,519
You took the law
into your own hands.

369
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:32,919
You killed your daughter's
murderer. Out of revenge.

370
00:27:34,679 --> 00:27:38,919
But above all, you wanted
the name of the other man.

371
00:27:39,959 --> 00:27:41,919
The one who was filming.

372
00:27:42,519 --> 00:27:45,719
And there was only one
person, who knew it: Albrecht.

373
00:27:46,639 --> 00:27:50,479
He has not voluntarily withdrawn 
himself from it. They had to kidnap him.

374
00:27:50,639 --> 00:27:52,679
And now that Albrecht is dead,

375
00:27:53,519 --> 00:27:55,999
you will know this name.
- No.

376
00:27:58,919 --> 00:28:00,879
It is entirely up to you.

377
00:28:01,039 --> 00:28:04,759
Tell me the name of the co-
conspirator, and I will have him arrested.

378
00:28:04,919 --> 00:28:07,239
He will come before a court
and be convicted.

379
00:28:07,399 --> 00:28:10,719
Dangerous, what you are planning.
- You would do that for me?

380
00:28:11,399 --> 00:28:14,039
I would do that for you.
- Danger is imminent.

381
00:28:14,199 --> 00:28:16,159
The question is, for whom.

382
00:28:16,439 --> 00:28:19,079
Who should testify to the complicity
of the man,

383
00:28:19,239 --> 00:28:21,679
when the only one who could do it
is dead?

384
00:28:21,839 --> 00:28:24,599
Mr. Mendt,
we always find something.

385
00:28:24,759 --> 00:28:28,599
An eyelash, a hair, skin flakes,
something - we'll find something.

386
00:28:29,799 --> 00:28:32,759
Unfortunately, I don't
know the name of this man.

387
00:28:35,279 --> 00:28:37,239
Hello.
- Hello.

388
00:28:37,399 --> 00:28:39,879
Mr. Bootz, do you have a moment?
- Yes.

389
00:28:43,679 --> 00:28:45,639
I know.

390
00:28:45,799 --> 00:28:48,759
You can't put the man
in pretrial detention.

391
00:28:48,959 --> 00:28:51,639
Your suspicion doesn't hold up.
- I'm well aware of that.

392
00:28:53,479 --> 00:28:55,439
(quietly:) Okay.

393
00:29:00,399 --> 00:29:03,199
Stuttgart District Attorney's Office.
I am Emilia Alvarez.

394
00:29:03,359 --> 00:29:05,319
Frank Mendt.

395
00:29:05,479 --> 00:29:07,639
Your arrest
was not justified.

396
00:29:07,799 --> 00:29:09,759
Commissioner Bootz
is taking you home.

397
00:29:09,959 --> 00:29:13,439
I'm sorry about the circumstances.
- Thank you, I'd rather walk.

398
00:29:13,599 --> 00:29:15,559
Goodbye.

399
00:29:20,359 --> 00:29:22,319
(quietly:) Come on, let's go.

400
00:29:23,159 --> 00:29:25,359
(Tense music)

401
00:29:37,799 --> 00:29:40,039
You shouldn't have let him go.

402
00:29:40,479 --> 00:29:42,439
No.

403
00:29:42,919 --> 00:29:45,599
You could have held him for 48 hours.

404
00:29:46,159 --> 00:29:48,359
What would we have gained?
- Time.

405
00:29:49,119 --> 00:29:51,279
Only to a limited extent.

406
00:29:51,439 --> 00:29:54,559
We would have had to tail him
fo r the rest of his life,

407
00:29:54,625 --> 00:29:57,825
to stop him from taking the law
into his own hands.

408
00:29:57,959 --> 00:30:00,839
Now we can directly
stop him from doing something foolish

409
00:30:00,999 --> 00:30:03,039
and catch the second man.

410
00:30:03,599 --> 00:30:06,159
He goes to the taxis.
- "Yes, I see him."

411
00:30:08,039 --> 00:30:10,079
Hello.

412
00:30:10,239 --> 00:30:13,079
Reinhard, you're taking one too!
Pursue him!

413
00:30:13,399 --> 00:30:15,359
"Quick, he's already leaving!"

414
00:30:17,799 --> 00:30:19,759
(Engine is started.)

415
00:30:23,639 --> 00:30:25,959
(Tense music)

416
00:30:31,039 --> 00:30:33,279
He's in a taxi heading south
on his way.

417
00:30:33,799 --> 00:30:36,759
Then he's not heading home.
- "Doesn't look like it."

418
00:30:37,079 --> 00:30:39,279
"Where are you?"
- I'll be right there.

419
00:30:43,239 --> 00:30:46,079
Reinhard, fall
back, I'll take over.

420
00:30:46,279 --> 00:30:48,239
Okay. Understood.

421
00:30:53,599 --> 00:30:55,559
Ms. Lothar, yes?

422
00:30:56,159 --> 00:30:59,159
Milena Lothar, yes.
- You're a trainee detective?

423
00:31:01,639 --> 00:31:04,359
Do you have a boyfriend?
- Daniel.

424
00:31:07,479 --> 00:31:11,159
Don't lose track of him
while chasing down criminals.

425
00:31:14,239 --> 00:31:16,199
(Barking)

426
00:31:18,119 --> 00:31:20,079
Oh, we're getting visitors.

427
00:31:20,599 --> 00:31:22,559
Hello.

428
00:31:22,719 --> 00:31:24,919
Lannert.
- Hello.

429
00:31:25,079 --> 00:31:27,039
Damn.
- Hello.

430
00:31:27,239 --> 00:31:29,199
Weigert.

431
00:31:30,279 --> 00:31:32,239
Visitors?
- No, nobody was here.

432
00:31:32,399 --> 00:31:34,359
She's not out either?
- Nope.

433
00:31:34,519 --> 00:31:36,759
Keeps wandering around
the house: lights on, lights off.

434
00:31:37,439 --> 00:31:39,639
(Tense music)

435
00:31:47,239 --> 00:31:49,839
They go where Mendt goes.
Discreetly.

436
00:31:49,999 --> 00:31:53,439
I'm always there, don't
worry. Watch your back, clear?

437
00:32:13,599 --> 00:32:16,039
It looks like he's
taking the funicular.

438
00:32:16,199 --> 00:32:18,559
(Reinhard:) "Inheritance Chaser Express."
- I beg your pardon?

439
00:32:18,719 --> 00:32:20,879
"He means the cable
car to the cemetery."."

440
00:32:21,119 --> 00:32:23,679
He's probably visiting Mareike's grave.
- "Could very well be."

441
00:32:24,039 --> 00:32:26,159
"Can you hear me, Reinhard?"
- Affirmative.

442
00:32:26,439 --> 00:32:30,279
If Mendt gets on, stay
below in case he comes back.

443
00:32:30,639 --> 00:32:33,372
"Mrs. Lothar, you're riding up."
- And you?

444
00:32:33,559 --> 00:32:36,139
"See you up there."
- "He's on board."

445
00:32:36,319 --> 00:32:38,279
"Colleague is following."

446
00:32:39,159 --> 00:32:41,639
(Murmuring, signal tone)

447
00:32:48,759 --> 00:32:51,959
Hm! What's this going to be?
- No idea.

448
00:32:56,199 --> 00:32:58,559
(Tense music)

449
00:33:19,479 --> 00:33:21,759
Not exactly "Lights On, Lights Off"!

450
00:34:09,559 --> 00:34:11,959
(Ominous music)

451
00:34:13,959 --> 00:34:15,919
Mrs. Mendt!

452
00:34:16,399 --> 00:34:18,359
Mrs. Mendt!

453
00:34:39,119 --> 00:34:41,359
Just went into a flower shop.

454
00:34:42,039 --> 00:34:44,119
(She chucks.)

455
00:34:44,639 --> 00:34:47,159
And, what did you say then?

456
00:34:50,439 --> 00:34:53,838
Heading to the cemetery right
now, I'm following. Where are you?

457
00:34:53,919 --> 00:34:55,879
"I'm on my way."

458
00:34:57,279 --> 00:34:59,639
Super!
When did you last see her?

459
00:34:59,799 --> 00:35:03,279
And if she's hiding?
- And where? In the washing machine?

460
00:35:03,439 --> 00:35:05,919
Maybe she's shopping.
- Of course, she said:

461
00:35:06,079 --> 00:35:09,039
Then I'll sneak
through the garden to the supermarket.

462
00:35:09,199 --> 00:35:13,039
Gentlemen, surveillance doesn't mean
sitting on your ass in the car!

463
00:35:13,199 --> 00:35:15,519
When did you last
see her?

464
00:35:15,719 --> 00:35:17,999
Oh, the light just turned on!

465
00:35:18,239 --> 00:35:20,999
Hopefully yours did too!
Those are timer switches!

466
00:35:21,159 --> 00:35:23,279
When did you last
see her?

467
00:35:23,439 --> 00:35:26,599
She was upstairs in the room once,
that was ... half an hour.

468
00:35:26,799 --> 00:35:29,279
Issue a missing person alert
for Simone Mendt immediately.

469
00:35:29,479 --> 00:35:31,479
Immediately!
- Yes.

470
00:35:32,439 --> 00:35:34,839
(Tense music)

471
00:35:56,719 --> 00:35:58,879
Have you lost him?
- Yes.

472
00:35:59,119 --> 00:36:01,239
He turned the
corner and was gone.

473
00:36:01,399 --> 00:36:03,359
Shit!

474
00:36:03,759 --> 00:36:05,919
(Phone rings.)

475
00:36:06,559 --> 00:36:08,519
Shit ...
- Hello?

476
00:36:08,759 --> 00:36:11,992
It's me. Simone Mendt
has gone missing.

477
00:36:12,319 --> 00:36:15,279
"Be careful that the same thing
doesn't happen to Mr. Mendt!"

478
00:36:15,439 --> 00:36:17,519
It just happened.
- Shit!

479
00:36:20,239 --> 00:36:24,192
What was it? Weigert and Teufel?
- Man, hey ...

480
00:36:24,838 --> 00:36:27,079
Man, fuck!

481
00:36:31,799 --> 00:36:34,119
(Soft, dark music)

482
00:36:52,519 --> 00:36:54,479
So?

483
00:36:54,639 --> 00:36:56,599
Yeah, I've got something.

484
00:36:56,759 --> 00:36:59,759
Mr. Mendt called a lawyer
from here earlier.

485
00:36:59,919 --> 00:37:02,239
Can you get the number?
- Yeah, sure.

486
00:37:05,519 --> 00:37:09,439
This is everything we have
in connection with Jörg Albrecht.

487
00:37:09,839 --> 00:37:11,799
So, where things stand.

488
00:37:11,959 --> 00:37:14,879
The Mendts are being sought
nationwide.

489
00:37:15,039 --> 00:37:17,999
The man involved in the abuse
probably has no idea

490
00:37:18,159 --> 00:37:20,239
that his life is in danger.

491
00:37:20,399 --> 00:37:23,679
And somewhere here is the clue
about this second man.

492
00:37:26,279 --> 00:37:28,479
We should be faster than them.

493
00:37:28,639 --> 00:37:30,599
The colleagues from back then

494
00:37:30,759 --> 00:37:33,359
focused on the members of the
biker club.

495
00:37:34,799 --> 00:37:36,759
Okay, let's narrow it down.

496
00:37:36,919 --> 00:37:40,319
Albrecht spent two years in
prison for animal cruelty and assault.

497
00:37:40,479 --> 00:37:42,799
A year before the murder
of Mareike he got out.

498
00:37:42,959 --> 00:37:45,239
And he joined the Devils.

499
00:37:45,399 --> 00:37:48,679
He met this guy in prison.
Stefan Freund.

500
00:37:48,879 --> 00:37:52,599
The number Mendt
dialed, is his own landline.

501
00:37:52,759 --> 00:37:55,239
He called his wife.
- And warned her.

502
00:37:55,399 --> 00:37:59,159
You tricked both of us.
- That strengthens the suspicion of murder.

503
00:37:59,319 --> 00:38:03,079
One more thing: I found in the ashtray
a small reflection

504
00:38:03,319 --> 00:38:05,839
from a hand of the person
who filmed.

505
00:38:05,999 --> 00:38:08,919
The computer still needs a bit of time.
- Let me know.

506
00:38:09,079 --> 00:38:11,199
Albrecht's new friends
are the Devils.

507
00:38:11,639 --> 00:38:14,079
Which one of them would
film an act of abuse

508
00:38:14,239 --> 00:38:17,399
and even putting him online,
to make money out of it?

509
00:38:17,559 --> 00:38:19,759
One of his new friends.

510
00:38:20,759 --> 00:38:23,159
That's the biker club Devils.

511
00:38:23,559 --> 00:38:26,439
Michael Kurzenberger got
drunk and drove to his death.

512
00:38:26,759 --> 00:38:30,279
Stefan Freund keeps
turning up for drug offenses.

513
00:38:30,439 --> 00:38:32,879
Lives on Hartz IV, here in Stuttgart.

514
00:38:33,679 --> 00:38:37,119
Joachim Huber now has
a bar in Untertürkheim.

515
00:38:37,599 --> 00:38:41,839
Matthias Lösel died in
Brittany in a knife fight.

516
00:38:42,039 --> 00:38:43,999
I've got something!

517
00:38:49,679 --> 00:38:52,759
Okay, take a look at the ashtray.

518
00:38:53,919 --> 00:38:56,559
Do you see that?
- Yes...

519
00:38:56,799 --> 00:39:00,679
On the ashtray, I found the
reflection of a man's hand.

520
00:39:01,079 --> 00:39:04,359
I interpolated the whole
thing, it took about two hours.

521
00:39:04,519 --> 00:39:06,479
Here's the result.

522
00:39:09,319 --> 00:39:11,479
A turtle or something ...
- Yes.

523
00:39:13,439 --> 00:39:15,719
(Soft, tense music)

524
00:39:19,519 --> 00:39:21,479
There.

525
00:39:24,839 --> 00:39:26,799
Stefan Freund.

526
00:39:29,959 --> 00:39:32,479
(Dark music)

527
00:39:34,279 --> 00:39:36,439
(Low conversation)

528
00:39:53,919 --> 00:39:56,039
Bye, Lena. See you tomorrow.

529
00:40:14,759 --> 00:40:17,159
Stefan Freund?
- Yes.

530
00:40:17,439 --> 00:40:20,759
My name is Lannert, Homicide
Stuttgart. My colleague Bootz.

531
00:40:20,919 --> 00:40:22,999
May we see
your hands for a moment?

532
00:40:23,199 --> 00:40:25,159
(He sniffs.)

533
00:40:29,268 --> 00:40:31,268
We're taking you into 
protective custody now.

534
00:40:31,292 --> 00:40:32,852
Protective custody? Why?

535
00:40:32,879 --> 00:40:35,119
Mareike Mendt, does
that mean anything to you?

536
00:40:35,319 --> 00:40:37,279
No.

537
00:40:37,304 --> 00:40:40,559
The colleagues are getting things
from the apartment. Come with me.

538
00:40:40,839 --> 00:40:42,799
(Siren)

539
00:40:43,159 --> 00:40:45,119
Thank you.

540
00:40:47,639 --> 00:40:49,599
(Engine is started.)

541
00:40:53,599 --> 00:40:55,919
(Tense music)

542
00:41:19,999 --> 00:41:22,119
Hi!
(Door is closed.)

543
00:41:22,759 --> 00:41:26,279
(Radio:) "... there may be
occasional sleet tonight."

544
00:41:26,439 --> 00:41:28,399
Maja?

545
00:41:32,599 --> 00:41:34,679
Leaving the lights on everywhere ...

546
00:41:40,199 --> 00:41:42,159
Maja?

547
00:41:44,199 --> 00:41:46,159
Are you hungry?

548
00:41:46,919 --> 00:41:48,959
I made you dinner!

549
00:41:49,439 --> 00:41:52,239
Yeah, I can see it! Wow!

550
00:41:52,439 --> 00:41:54,399
(Music from the radio)

551
00:42:00,519 --> 00:42:02,479
Whoa, that looks delicious!

552
00:42:02,919 --> 00:42:05,839
Do you think you can send
me to the party like this?

553
00:42:06,879 --> 00:42:08,839
You really are something!

554
00:42:09,039 --> 00:42:12,079
Change your clothes, I'll drive you.
- Anna's mother is driving us.

555
00:42:12,239 --> 00:42:14,519
I hadn't even said yes yet!
(Doorbell)

556
00:42:14,679 --> 00:42:16,639
That's Anna!
- Hey, um...

557
00:42:16,839 --> 00:42:18,919
Yes?
- I'll pick you up tomorrow morning.

558
00:42:19,079 --> 00:42:21,039
Okay, thanks!
- You're welcome.

559
00:42:21,239 --> 00:42:23,199
And thanks for the food.

560
00:42:23,359 --> 00:42:25,319
You're welcome!
- Take care!

561
00:42:25,479 --> 00:42:27,439
I will!
(Door slams shut.)

562
00:42:28,679 --> 00:42:30,879
(Calm pop music)

563
00:42:58,919 --> 00:43:00,879
(Laughter, soft pop music)

564
00:43:02,359 --> 00:43:04,319
Hello, Anna.

565
00:43:05,279 --> 00:43:07,839
Hello.
- Is Maja still in there?

566
00:43:07,999 --> 00:43:10,519
She wanted to surprise
you, with breakfast.

567
00:43:10,679 --> 00:43:13,799
Oh, I see? When did she leave?
- Half past six?

568
00:43:14,039 --> 00:43:15,999
Half past six?

569
00:43:16,399 --> 00:43:18,359
Weird...

570
00:43:18,559 --> 00:43:21,399
She wanted to go straight home.
- Yes. Isn't she at home?

571
00:43:21,559 --> 00:43:23,719
Nah, but that doesn't mean a thing.

572
00:43:23,879 --> 00:43:25,839
I'll give her a call.

573
00:43:30,759 --> 00:43:32,839
(Man:) "Yeah?"
- Who's there?

574
00:43:32,999 --> 00:43:35,359
"You know who's
here, Mr. Bootz."

575
00:43:35,719 --> 00:43:37,679
(Eerie music)

576
00:43:38,679 --> 00:43:41,119
Where is my daughter?
- "She's with me."

577
00:43:41,279 --> 00:43:43,799
"She's sleeping."
- What do you want?

578
00:43:44,959 --> 00:43:46,919
"Stefan Freund."

579
00:43:50,999 --> 00:43:53,159
"I'm checking in."
(Dial tone)

580
00:44:00,319 --> 00:44:02,279
Shit ...

581
00:44:05,599 --> 00:44:07,799
(He breathes rapidly.)

582
00:44:15,799 --> 00:44:18,919
This is Basti. I need a cell
phone trace immediately.

583
00:44:19,079 --> 00:44:22,359
My daughter,
who ... lost her phone.

584
00:44:22,519 --> 00:44:24,959
It's just gone.
Can you do that?

585
00:44:26,759 --> 00:44:29,639
(Atmospheric,
tense music)

586
00:44:45,119 --> 00:44:47,239
(Distant siren)

587
00:45:17,319 --> 00:45:20,799
The first signal came about 20
minutes ago, right here in Wangen.

588
00:45:20,999 --> 00:45:23,839
The second one five
minutes ago, near Villa Berg.

589
00:45:24,159 --> 00:45:26,719
And since then, your
daughter's phone has been dead.

590
00:45:26,879 --> 00:45:29,439
It has apparently
changed hands.

591
00:45:29,599 --> 00:45:32,519
Let me know immediately
when it stops moving.

592
00:45:32,679 --> 00:45:36,359
Yeah, but I've got other things to do.
- Hey, this is extremely important!

593
00:45:36,519 --> 00:45:39,799
There's sensitive data on it, okay?
So just do it.

594
00:45:41,479 --> 00:45:43,439
Morning.
- Good morning.

595
00:45:43,599 --> 00:45:45,679
Anything new from the Mends?
- No.

596
00:45:48,639 --> 00:45:50,599
Good morning.
- Good morning.

597
00:45:50,759 --> 00:45:53,119
Do you have any new leads
from the Mends?

598
00:45:53,519 --> 00:45:56,759
Uh, no. But I've
raised the alert level.

599
00:45:57,039 --> 00:45:58,999
What?

600
00:46:00,399 --> 00:46:02,359
Raised? Why raise it?
- What, why?

601
00:46:02,679 --> 00:46:06,159
Because one of them or both
of them murdered Jörg Albrecht.

602
00:46:06,919 --> 00:46:09,519
But that's not even
proven yet.

603
00:46:09,679 --> 00:46:11,959
Why did the two of
them disappear yesterday?

604
00:46:12,119 --> 00:46:14,079
It's as good as proven.

605
00:46:14,239 --> 00:46:17,999
The forensic team searched
the Mends' house last night.

606
00:46:18,159 --> 00:46:21,959
They found hair and skin particles in the
basement and on the stairs.

607
00:46:22,159 --> 00:46:24,159
Jörg Albrecht was definitely there.

608
00:46:26,439 --> 00:46:29,399
It seems to me an undercover search
would be more sensible.

609
00:46:31,959 --> 00:46:33,919
Aha ...

610
00:46:34,679 --> 00:46:38,079
Apparently, the Mends have launched their
private crusade for revenge.

611
00:46:38,239 --> 00:46:40,199
They murdered Albrecht.

612
00:46:40,599 --> 00:46:42,679
But if he told them,

613
00:46:42,839 --> 00:46:45,519
that it's Stefan Freund,
before he died,

614
00:46:45,959 --> 00:46:47,919
the one they're looking for.

615
00:46:48,079 --> 00:46:50,439
Then the story is
over here.

616
00:46:50,639 --> 00:46:54,279
We have Freund. Sooner or later
the Mends will fall into our net.

617
00:46:54,439 --> 00:46:56,519
So they're no longer a threat?

618
00:46:56,679 --> 00:47:00,399
They never were to the public.
They did what they wanted to do.

619
00:47:00,559 --> 00:47:03,359
Nothing suggests
that they're going on a rampage now.

620
00:47:03,519 --> 00:47:05,799
But they're probably murderers.
- Exactly.

621
00:47:05,999 --> 00:47:09,279
That's why I'm concerned
about the risk to bystanders.

622
00:47:10,119 --> 00:47:13,319
The Mendts are on the run
for the first time in their lives.

623
00:47:13,479 --> 00:47:15,999
That is real psychological
stress for them.

624
00:47:16,279 --> 00:47:19,239
Anything could happen.
Especially when ...

625
00:47:19,399 --> 00:47:22,719
... Officer Norbert from Klein
Gartbach wants to arrest them.

626
00:47:22,999 --> 00:47:25,199
Hold on,
what's this really about?

627
00:47:25,359 --> 00:47:27,319
What I'm trying to say is:

628
00:47:27,599 --> 00:47:31,519
I just want us to scale this down to
a covert search.

629
00:47:31,679 --> 00:47:34,919
The manhunt is active,
but whoever knows anything about Mends,

630
00:47:35,079 --> 00:47:37,039
they call us here.

631
00:47:37,199 --> 00:47:39,439
I see no problem with that.
- Mhm.

632
00:47:39,599 --> 00:47:41,559
Then I'll arrange it.

633
00:47:41,719 --> 00:47:43,759
Maybe they're already
abroad.

634
00:47:43,959 --> 00:47:46,279
No, they're still here.
In the Stuttgart area.

635
00:47:46,479 --> 00:47:49,199
They can't just
vanish into thin air.

636
00:47:49,359 --> 00:47:52,559
They have to eat, sleep,
shop. Contact other people.

637
00:47:52,719 --> 00:47:55,519
They have no idea
about living on the run.

638
00:47:55,679 --> 00:47:58,159
They'll make mistakes.
Leave traces.

639
00:47:58,319 --> 00:48:01,599
We can take another look
around their house. Shall we?

640
00:48:02,039 --> 00:48:05,719
You go. I'll look into everything else
: bank details, phone connections,

641
00:48:05,879 --> 00:48:08,319
social circle.
That way we're more efficient.

642
00:48:10,239 --> 00:48:12,519
Can you convince a judge
that

643
00:48:12,679 --> 00:48:14,719
we can get access
to the accounts?

644
00:48:15,079 --> 00:48:17,119
That's already been done.
I'll press further.

645
00:48:27,639 --> 00:48:30,439
So, see you then.
- Let me know if you find anything.

646
00:48:30,599 --> 00:48:32,559
Yeah.

647
00:48:34,199 --> 00:48:36,199
Everything good with you?

648
00:48:39,519 --> 00:48:41,479
(He sighs.)

649
00:48:45,159 --> 00:48:47,479
(Distant siren)

650
00:48:50,839 --> 00:48:53,079
(Quiet, tense music)

651
00:49:03,239 --> 00:49:05,359
Sorry about earlier.
Anything new?

652
00:49:09,399 --> 00:49:11,439
Yeah.
- Yeah?

653
00:49:11,759 --> 00:49:13,719
Yeah.

654
00:49:14,359 --> 00:49:16,519
Here. This is new.

655
00:49:16,679 --> 00:49:18,639
Killesberg ...
- Mhm.

656
00:49:18,879 --> 00:49:20,839
And now, in this moment?

657
00:49:20,999 --> 00:49:24,399
It's over. Sebastian, what's
actually going on with you?

658
00:49:24,559 --> 00:49:26,519
(Mobile phone rings.)

659
00:49:26,679 --> 00:49:28,639
Everything's fine.

660
00:49:29,359 --> 00:49:32,319
I have to take this real quick.
I'll call back in a bit.

661
00:49:41,239 --> 00:49:43,319
Hello?
- (Woman:) "Sebastian?"

662
00:49:43,599 --> 00:49:46,599
"It just rained. We're already
on our way back today."

663
00:49:46,639 --> 00:49:48,799
What?
- "Do you want me to bring Maja over?"

664
00:49:48,959 --> 00:49:51,759
"I'm making flatbread.
You're of course invited."

665
00:49:54,439 --> 00:49:57,239
"Sebastian?"
- Yes, yes, yes. I, um ...

666
00:49:58,079 --> 00:50:00,839
I'm still on it. Um ...
Where are you now?

667
00:50:01,079 --> 00:50:04,279
"At Moritz's place. He and Henri
won't be coming until tomorrow."

668
00:50:04,639 --> 00:50:07,079
I see. I ... I'll stop by.

669
00:50:08,599 --> 00:50:11,039
(Quiet, tense music)

670
00:50:15,919 --> 00:50:17,879
I'll call you.

671
00:50:24,159 --> 00:50:26,599
(Quiet, uneasy music)

672
00:50:37,559 --> 00:50:39,679
(Fast music)

673
00:50:42,959 --> 00:50:44,919
(Honking)

674
00:50:48,719 --> 00:50:50,719
(Mobile phone rings.)

675
00:51:02,879 --> 00:51:04,839
Yes? Hello?

676
00:51:05,039 --> 00:51:07,319
(Mendt:) "So, how does it feel?"

677
00:51:07,479 --> 00:51:10,679
"When you no longer
lecture another father

678
00:51:10,839 --> 00:51:12,799
on what right and wrong are?"

679
00:51:12,959 --> 00:51:15,319
"On
whether his suffering permits him

680
00:51:15,479 --> 00:51:17,919
to place himself above the law?"
- Not good.

681
00:51:18,119 --> 00:51:20,079
It doesn't feel good.

682
00:51:20,439 --> 00:51:23,759
"In an hour I'll tell you
where to deliver Freund."

683
00:51:25,119 --> 00:51:27,959
"And you can have your daughter
back unharmed."

684
00:51:28,199 --> 00:51:30,279
"The chance I never had."

685
00:51:30,799 --> 00:51:32,759
"It's entirely up to you."

686
00:51:35,559 --> 00:51:39,039
"From now on I'll only be
calling from a prepaid phone."

687
00:51:41,319 --> 00:51:44,119
But what ... what will you
do to Mr. Freund?

688
00:51:44,479 --> 00:51:47,079
Execute him? Take his life?

689
00:51:47,799 --> 00:51:52,199
"My daughter was ...
abused through all of her body orifices."

690
00:51:53,839 --> 00:51:56,079
"Had she not been strangled,

691
00:51:56,279 --> 00:51:59,119
she would have died from the internal
bleeding."

692
00:52:00,719 --> 00:52:03,959
"This unspeakable martyrdom
lives in our minds."

693
00:52:04,919 --> 00:52:08,359
"And my wife and I.
It governs our daily life."

694
00:52:08,599 --> 00:52:10,799
"It occupies us day and night."

695
00:52:11,199 --> 00:52:14,639
"For 15 years. Now I'm going to
put an end to this torment."

696
00:52:14,919 --> 00:52:17,839
I'm sorry. I'm truly
sorry, Mr. Mendt.

697
00:52:17,999 --> 00:52:20,399
I know, it's terrible, I ...
But ...

698
00:52:20,759 --> 00:52:24,239
If I don't give you a friend
and you take my daughter from me,

699
00:52:24,399 --> 00:52:26,359
what are you going to do?

700
00:52:26,519 --> 00:52:29,719
Do you and your wife simply want
to keep a marriage going? How?

701
00:52:29,879 --> 00:52:31,919
"I certainly don't want that."

702
00:52:32,839 --> 00:52:34,799
"Then we're leaving too."

703
00:52:35,159 --> 00:52:37,559
(Tense music)

704
00:52:41,279 --> 00:52:43,239
"In an hour, yes."

705
00:52:44,959 --> 00:52:46,919
(Bird call)

706
00:53:02,759 --> 00:53:05,279
(Soft, calm music)

707
00:53:18,559 --> 00:53:20,519
(Doorbell)

708
00:53:20,879 --> 00:53:23,799
You're quick. The flame
pie is not ready yet.

709
00:53:24,799 --> 00:53:27,799
Your guy isn't here, is he?
- What? No.

710
00:53:28,039 --> 00:53:30,079
And Henri? Where is Henri?
- No.

711
00:53:30,279 --> 00:53:32,679
I did say
they're not coming until tomorrow.

712
00:53:34,199 --> 00:53:36,159
What's going on?

713
00:53:37,039 --> 00:53:39,399
(He's breathing hard.)

714
00:53:40,199 --> 00:53:42,159
What happened to Maja?

715
00:53:47,919 --> 00:53:49,879
She's been kidnapped.
- What?

716
00:53:50,119 --> 00:53:52,719
By a married couple
who had a daughter of their own.

717
00:53:52,999 --> 00:53:55,999
The... Fifteen years ago she was
kidnapped, she...

718
00:53:56,919 --> 00:53:59,679
... was abused
by two perpetrators.

719
00:53:59,959 --> 00:54:02,719
Then one of them got out,
and the one who...

720
00:54:02,879 --> 00:54:04,839
They took revenge on him.

721
00:54:04,999 --> 00:54:08,959
They want the other one, but
we have him, that's why they have Maja.

722
00:54:09,559 --> 00:54:12,559
When did this happen?
- This morning? I'm not exactly sure.

723
00:54:12,719 --> 00:54:14,879
Maja wanted to go to
this sleepover party,

724
00:54:15,039 --> 00:54:17,319
and I actually said no.

725
00:54:17,639 --> 00:54:19,799
She ended up
talking me into it.

726
00:54:19,959 --> 00:54:22,599
She was allowed to go, I wanted
to pick her up in the morning.

727
00:54:22,759 --> 00:54:24,719
And she was gone.

728
00:54:24,879 --> 00:54:26,919
Did they let you
talk to her?

729
00:54:27,079 --> 00:54:29,319
No, but she's doing fine,
I know that.

730
00:54:29,519 --> 00:54:32,079
How do you know that?
- Because I know it!

731
00:54:32,759 --> 00:54:34,799
How do they even know about Maja?

732
00:54:35,279 --> 00:54:37,639
Because I told him, of course.

733
00:54:37,799 --> 00:54:40,479
You told him?
- Yeah, he had asked me.

734
00:54:40,639 --> 00:54:44,479
Because he also had a daughter,
and I said, I have a daughter too.

735
00:54:44,639 --> 00:54:47,439
Shit, I gotta go!
- I'm coming with you.

736
00:54:48,639 --> 00:54:51,079
You're not coming with me!
- Of course I'm coming.

737
00:54:51,239 --> 00:54:53,559
No!
- Am I supposed to just sit here, or what?

738
00:54:53,719 --> 00:54:56,839
That's not possible! You can't
come with me! It doesn't work!

739
00:54:56,999 --> 00:54:59,359
That's not possible! They're
pulling me off the case!

740
00:54:59,559 --> 00:55:02,519
I can't do anything
anymore, take care of you.

741
00:55:02,759 --> 00:55:05,479
This other offender.
Can't you just swap them out, right?

742
00:55:05,639 --> 00:55:07,599
W... What, how?

743
00:55:08,119 --> 00:55:10,759
Yeah, swap them out.
- Yeah, but then he's dead.

744
00:55:10,919 --> 00:55:13,319
He's dead!
- And what do you want to do then?

745
00:55:13,479 --> 00:55:15,439
What would you even do?

746
00:55:15,599 --> 00:55:18,479
You'd just hand the man over to them
for your daughter, wouldn't you?

747
00:55:18,639 --> 00:55:21,319
There's no way you would,
not for even one second ...

748
00:55:21,479 --> 00:55:25,159
There has to be another way! Should I
put a bullet in his head?

749
00:55:25,319 --> 00:55:27,559
What are you going to do?
- I'll save her.

750
00:55:28,839 --> 00:55:31,319
I'll pull it off.
I'll find a way.

751
00:55:31,599 --> 00:55:33,559
I'll call you.

752
00:55:35,559 --> 00:55:37,519
(Dark music)

753
00:55:54,759 --> 00:55:56,959
(Engine noise, barking)

754
00:55:59,719 --> 00:56:01,799
(Tense music)

755
00:56:02,639 --> 00:56:04,599
I'm up here!

756
00:56:04,759 --> 00:56:06,719
Sebastian!

757
00:56:13,039 --> 00:56:15,079
Did you find anything?

758
00:56:16,119 --> 00:56:18,839
They've set up her daughter's room
so perfectly,

759
00:56:18,999 --> 00:56:21,719
as if she were to come home
any moment now.

760
00:56:21,879 --> 00:56:23,839
They're not done yet.

761
00:56:23,999 --> 00:56:26,559
They haven't come to
terms with their grief yet.

762
00:56:26,719 --> 00:56:29,879
That will only happen
once Freund is convicted.

763
00:56:32,119 --> 00:56:34,079
What's going on?

764
00:56:34,399 --> 00:56:36,479
(He's breathing heavily.)

765
00:56:41,439 --> 00:56:43,479
I, um ...

766
00:56:47,079 --> 00:56:49,639
You have to promise
me something, Thorsten.

767
00:56:50,519 --> 00:56:52,879
You need to keep this to yourself,
okay?

768
00:56:53,399 --> 00:56:56,559
I don't want to be
pulled off this case.

769
00:56:58,199 --> 00:57:00,519
The Mendts have kidnapped Maja.

770
00:57:00,719 --> 00:57:03,919
What?
- Yes. They kidnapped Maja.

771
00:57:04,079 --> 00:57:06,239
That's not true, is it?
- It is.

772
00:57:06,399 --> 00:57:08,359
You've got to be kidding!

773
00:57:08,679 --> 00:57:11,959
They want me to hand over
Stefan Freund in exchange for her.

774
00:57:12,119 --> 00:57:14,959
Then they'll let her go.
- This can't be right!

775
00:57:15,119 --> 00:57:17,799
But it is!
- Do you know where she might be?

776
00:57:18,159 --> 00:57:20,119
M-m. No.

777
00:57:21,079 --> 00:57:23,039
And when?

778
00:57:24,359 --> 00:57:26,319
They, um....

779
00:57:27,239 --> 00:57:29,879
Forty-five minutes.
Then he'll check in again.

780
00:57:30,079 --> 00:57:32,119
That's why we're not going public.

781
00:57:33,399 --> 00:57:35,559
Nobody knows what they're planning.

782
00:57:36,319 --> 00:57:39,439
If they're under pressure,
anything could happen.

783
00:57:39,599 --> 00:57:41,679
Or some dumb cop
shoots at them.

784
00:57:41,839 --> 00:57:44,519
Who's going to tell me
where my daughter is? Shit!

785
00:57:44,759 --> 00:57:47,119
We need a full-scale manhunt now.
- No!

786
00:57:47,143 --> 00:57:49,183
No full-scale manhunt,
are you out of your mind?

787
00:57:49,208 --> 00:57:52,574
How are we supposed to find them on our own?
- I thought that ...

788
00:57:52,599 --> 00:57:55,439
... that maybe you would
... Fuck, I don't know!

789
00:57:55,599 --> 00:57:58,039
In any other case it'd
be a full-scale manhunt.

790
00:57:58,239 --> 00:58:00,479
This is no ordinary case!
- Yeah, I know!

791
00:58:02,479 --> 00:58:05,039
We need to go to Nika.
There must be a lead.

792
00:58:05,559 --> 00:58:08,599
If Mendt wants to have
Freund, he has to show his face.

793
00:58:08,759 --> 00:58:10,719
So, come on.

794
00:58:11,319 --> 00:58:13,279
Come on, let's go now!

795
00:58:13,439 --> 00:58:15,399
(He sighs.)

796
00:58:17,239 --> 00:58:20,239
Hey, any news?
- Not yet. Any with you?

797
00:58:20,919 --> 00:58:22,879
No.

798
00:58:22,992 --> 00:58:27,332
The PC and the credit cards haven't been used,
and the phones are dead. Unfortunately.

799
00:58:29,799 --> 00:58:31,759
There's a problem.

800
00:58:32,079 --> 00:58:34,039
What is it?

801
00:58:34,199 --> 00:58:37,239
The Mends want Stefan Freund,
to get their revenge on him.

802
00:58:38,159 --> 00:58:41,159
Because they can't get their
hands on him, they've been ...

803
00:58:42,159 --> 00:58:45,279
... they have kidnapped Sebastian's
daughter and are extorting him.

804
00:58:45,479 --> 00:58:47,479
What?
- Are you out of your mind?

805
00:58:47,639 --> 00:58:49,599
What is this?
- Stop it!

806
00:58:49,759 --> 00:58:51,719
Stop it!
- For God's sake!

807
00:58:51,879 --> 00:58:54,199
You don't have a
daughter left to lose!

808
00:58:54,399 --> 00:58:56,519
Pull yourself together!
- Come back!

809
00:58:56,799 --> 00:58:59,479
Mr. Bootz, please! Please!

810
00:59:00,199 --> 00:59:03,439
You promised me!
- I never promised you anything!

811
00:59:03,599 --> 00:59:05,559
Just stop it!

812
00:59:05,799 --> 00:59:08,799
Remove Mr. Bootz
from the case due to bias.

813
00:59:08,959 --> 00:59:11,479
You promised me!
- I didn't say a thing!

814
00:59:11,679 --> 00:59:13,799
Cut the crap!
- Is that true?

815
00:59:15,279 --> 00:59:17,239
You foul woman!

816
00:59:19,999 --> 00:59:21,959
Are you insane?

817
00:59:22,159 --> 00:59:25,199
You are Maya's father,
you ... You are biased!

818
00:59:25,359 --> 00:59:28,279
You can't handle this case.
- Why not?

819
00:59:29,559 --> 00:59:31,519
(He sniffs.)

820
00:59:31,679 --> 00:59:34,959
Hand over your service
weapon and badge immediately.

821
00:59:35,679 --> 00:59:38,439
You are temporarily
relieved of duty.

822
00:59:41,679 --> 00:59:43,999
Thank you. Thank you very much.

823
00:59:47,359 --> 00:59:49,639
The badge.
- I don't have it with me.

824
00:59:50,319 --> 00:59:53,039
I don't have my badge
with me, it's at home.

825
00:59:53,199 --> 00:59:55,159
You can send someone.

826
00:59:55,479 --> 00:59:58,199
You stay here and help
with the investigation.

827
00:59:58,519 --> 01:00:00,559
As a father, not as a detective!

828
01:00:00,999 --> 01:00:03,159
We need a photo for the manhunt.

829
01:00:03,319 --> 01:00:06,319
No manhunt! I won't allow
it! It puts them in danger!

830
01:00:06,405 --> 01:00:09,134
You're putting them in danger!
Only a large-scale manhunt will help!

831
01:00:09,159 --> 01:00:11,879
Someone must have
seen the Mendts or her.

832
01:00:12,039 --> 01:00:14,799
Please, no manhunt! The Mendts
don't know a thing about that.

833
01:00:14,959 --> 01:00:17,479
They're under so much
pressure! Don't do this!

834
01:00:17,639 --> 01:00:19,599
Mr. Bootz!

835
01:00:19,759 --> 01:00:23,719
If a man comes to you whose daughter
has been kidnapped, what do you do?

836
01:00:25,079 --> 01:00:27,039
Fuck ...

837
01:00:30,439 --> 01:00:32,399
(sobbing:) What the hell is going on!

838
01:00:35,639 --> 01:00:39,439
If a man were to come to you whose
daughter has just been kidnapped,

839
01:00:39,639 --> 01:00:42,599
you would immediately
launch a massive search!

840
01:00:43,959 --> 01:00:45,919
That you're not doing it now,

841
01:00:46,079 --> 01:00:49,559
because you assess the danger to
your daughter so differently,

842
01:00:49,719 --> 01:00:52,399
because you're the one affected, shows
how right it is

843
01:00:52,639 --> 01:00:55,039
not to leave the decision
up to you.

844
01:00:55,799 --> 01:00:57,839
What about the photo?

845
01:00:58,039 --> 01:01:01,199
Do you have one, or should I
take it out of the desk?

846
01:01:01,359 --> 01:01:03,319
(Sobbing)

847
01:01:03,479 --> 01:01:06,599
Do we have any leads
on where she is?

848
01:01:06,759 --> 01:01:09,559
No.
- And where are the Mendts?

849
01:01:09,759 --> 01:01:13,439
They'll only show themselves
once we hand Freund over to them.

850
01:01:13,799 --> 01:01:15,759
Okay.

851
01:01:15,919 --> 01:01:18,959
You're releasing the manhunt
data including Mrs. Banovic now.

852
01:01:19,119 --> 01:01:21,079
Age, height, and clothing.

853
01:01:21,239 --> 01:01:24,599
Also for the Mendts. Reasons for the
manhunt: Murder and child abduction.

854
01:01:24,759 --> 01:01:26,839
Out immediately,
to all departments.

855
01:01:26,999 --> 01:01:29,959
Immediately to regional and
national TV news.

856
01:01:30,119 --> 01:01:32,719
Also the online press, radio.

857
01:01:32,879 --> 01:01:35,119
To all airport staff,
taxi drivers.

858
01:01:35,279 --> 01:01:38,679
I want that within an hour
everyone knows who Maja Bootz is.

859
01:01:38,839 --> 01:01:41,014
You can put everyone
in the building to work.

860
01:01:41,039 --> 01:01:43,959
If we don't find Sebastian's daughter
and the Mends,

861
01:01:44,119 --> 01:01:46,239
we'll have to stage
a handover.

862
01:01:46,399 --> 01:01:50,319
And carry it out with full force.
- Yes, I'm counting on you.

863
01:01:51,439 --> 01:01:54,399
Sebastian, I need
the biometric data.

864
01:01:57,159 --> 01:01:59,999
Brown eyes, brown hair,
Height: 1.52.

865
01:02:01,639 --> 01:02:04,279
Mr. Bootz! Mr. Bootz, please,
the search data!

866
01:02:04,439 --> 01:02:06,399
Please!

867
01:02:07,999 --> 01:02:10,439
(Soft, tense music)

868
01:02:16,039 --> 01:02:18,239
It was right,
what you did.

869
01:02:18,399 --> 01:02:20,359
Let's hope so.

870
01:02:20,679 --> 01:02:24,199
(Radio:) "The weather for Württemberg,
from the Alps to the Main."

871
01:02:24,999 --> 01:02:27,199
"Snow or sleet,
lots of clouds,

872
01:02:27,359 --> 01:02:29,519
at minus one to plus three degrees."

873
01:02:29,679 --> 01:02:32,279
"Another important appeal
from the Stuttgart Police."

874
01:02:32,439 --> 01:02:35,399
"Maja Bootz, 13, is wanted,
brown hair, brown eyes,

875
01:02:35,559 --> 01:02:37,959
black jeans and a red puffer jacket."

876
01:02:38,119 --> 01:02:41,599
"In a few minutes I'll have
the event tips for you."

877
01:02:43,639 --> 01:02:46,359
"SWR3 until twelve -
the morning show!"

878
01:02:46,519 --> 01:02:49,999
"At the microphone Michael Reufsteck,
hello. We're collecting backups ..."

879
01:02:51,719 --> 01:02:53,679
(Typing)

880
01:02:54,359 --> 01:02:56,319
She's 13, right?

881
01:02:56,479 --> 01:02:58,439
(Dark music)

882
01:02:58,599 --> 01:03:00,559
(Typing)

883
01:03:09,959 --> 01:03:12,359
Today at Mendt's
I noticed something else,

884
01:03:12,519 --> 01:03:14,559
that might help us further.

885
01:03:15,159 --> 01:03:17,959
In a vacation photo
a motorhome can be seen.

886
01:03:18,599 --> 01:03:22,279
It could be that they still
have it and are on the road with it.

887
01:03:24,119 --> 01:03:26,519
I'll call the vehicle registration
office.

888
01:03:32,959 --> 01:03:34,919
(Door closed.)

889
01:03:37,959 --> 01:03:40,359
(Quiet, oppressive music)

890
01:03:41,359 --> 01:03:43,319
(Bird cries)

891
01:03:52,759 --> 01:03:54,719
Lannert.
- Karle.

892
01:03:54,879 --> 01:03:56,919
I'm glad you could make it.

893
01:04:03,399 --> 01:04:05,359
I need a man around forty.

894
01:04:05,519 --> 01:04:08,399
Hand-to-hand training,
single. He'll be Stefan Freund.

895
01:04:08,559 --> 01:04:10,519
I know someone for that.

896
01:04:10,759 --> 01:04:13,079
The two of them are
in a state of emergency.

897
01:04:13,759 --> 01:04:17,359
The world, they think, has
taken no note of their pain.

898
01:04:17,719 --> 01:04:19,999
And now they go
and set a beacon.

899
01:04:20,159 --> 01:04:22,919
Show the world the pain,
that they have suffered.

900
01:04:23,079 --> 01:04:25,039
Now the world shall suffer.

901
01:04:26,159 --> 01:04:29,279
That they drag a girl to her death,
they shut it out.

902
01:04:29,439 --> 01:04:31,399
They even have to.

903
01:04:31,559 --> 01:04:34,479
They don't want to kill Maja,
they want Stefan Freund.

904
01:04:34,639 --> 01:04:37,439
But if we think
we can outsmart them,

905
01:04:37,599 --> 01:04:40,199
because they won't harm my colleague's daughter,

906
01:04:40,359 --> 01:04:42,999
then they will
give us a very harsh wake-up call.

907
01:04:44,239 --> 01:04:47,119
They already felt
betrayed by the world.

908
01:04:47,279 --> 01:04:49,639
They won't let that
happen to them again.

909
01:04:49,839 --> 01:04:52,359
So the final rescue shot?
- Absolutely not.

910
01:04:53,239 --> 01:04:56,119
Fire authorization only
on my express orders.

911
01:04:56,279 --> 01:04:58,319
And if so, then only hand or legs.

912
01:04:58,479 --> 01:05:01,479
We need to find the girl,
and if we kill Mendt,

913
01:05:01,639 --> 01:05:03,679
then we might
never find out.

914
01:05:07,079 --> 01:05:09,039
Then the hand is gone.

915
01:05:11,199 --> 01:05:13,319
What do you
normally use it for?

916
01:05:13,479 --> 01:05:15,439
Against misunderstandings.

917
01:05:15,599 --> 01:05:17,559
(He sighs.)

918
01:05:18,879 --> 01:05:21,719
S, I, Z, 2306.
Great, thanks!

919
01:05:22,319 --> 01:05:25,439
Thorsten was right:
They have a motorhome.

920
01:05:26,079 --> 01:05:28,039
Okay, so.

921
01:05:28,199 --> 01:05:30,959
We're looking for a vehicle
with the license plate SIZ-2306.

922
01:05:31,119 --> 01:05:33,079
(Cell phone rings.)

923
01:05:33,239 --> 01:05:36,479
SIZ-2306, the owners are Mendt.
- No problem.

924
01:05:37,279 --> 01:05:39,359
(Suspenseful music)

925
01:05:44,399 --> 01:05:46,679
Yes?
- (Mendt:) "Do you have him?"

926
01:05:48,799 --> 01:05:50,759
Not yet. But I'll get him.

927
01:05:51,919 --> 01:05:54,839
At 12.30 I'm standing by
for exactly two minutes ...

928
01:05:55,399 --> 01:05:57,359
"... on the Max-Eyth-Steg."

929
01:05:58,119 --> 01:06:00,919
"Do you understand?"
- Yes, I understand.

930
01:06:01,399 --> 01:06:03,359
"Good."

931
01:06:10,399 --> 01:06:13,519
We still have about 20 minutes
to find the motorhome.

932
01:06:13,679 --> 01:06:15,639
Okay ...

933
01:06:16,399 --> 01:06:18,359
Mendt has checked in.

934
01:06:18,519 --> 01:06:21,079
He'll be there in 20 minutes
at the Max-Eyth-Steg.

935
01:06:21,239 --> 01:06:24,959
The car is in the underground parking.
A Mr. Karle from the SEK is inside.

936
01:06:25,119 --> 01:06:27,079
It will be Stefan Freund.

937
01:06:27,679 --> 01:06:30,479
And that's your plan?
- You drive with Karle there,

938
01:06:30,639 --> 01:06:34,239
you can deliver him, but you must
insist on seeing Maja.

939
01:06:34,439 --> 01:06:36,679
No visual contact, no exchange.
- And then?

940
01:06:36,839 --> 01:06:40,359
Then you insist on contact.
If not at the Steg, then somewhere else.

941
01:06:40,519 --> 01:06:43,039
On contact: engage.
There's no other way.

942
01:06:43,199 --> 01:06:45,159
Is there a catch?
- No!

943
01:06:45,319 --> 01:06:48,639
Once we find the RV,
we'll hit both locations.

944
01:06:48,839 --> 01:06:51,839
Your plan is shit. What if
they happen to have a photo?

945
01:06:52,079 --> 01:06:54,199
Then they'll see
we're fucking with them!

946
01:06:54,359 --> 01:06:56,399
Then my daughter's dead,
Thorsten.

947
01:06:56,559 --> 01:07:00,319
Then tell me how you'd do it,
and we'll do it exactly that way.

948
01:07:00,719 --> 01:07:03,519
So, what's your plan?
Because you don't have one.

949
01:07:04,839 --> 01:07:06,799
You want to turn in a friend.

950
01:07:06,959 --> 01:07:09,679
You might as well just shoot him
in the head yourself.

951
01:07:09,839 --> 01:07:13,279
I want my daughter back!
You should know how that feels!

952
01:07:13,479 --> 01:07:15,479
Yes! But if you hand that man
over,

953
01:07:15,639 --> 01:07:17,919
you're knowingly sending
him to his death.

954
01:07:18,119 --> 01:07:20,159
At least not my daughter.

955
01:07:20,359 --> 01:07:22,639
Yeah, exactly. That's your plan.

956
01:07:22,799 --> 01:07:24,759
I'm downstairs.

957
01:07:24,919 --> 01:07:26,959
I shouldn't have told you.

958
01:07:31,319 --> 01:07:33,439
(Soft, tense music)

959
01:07:34,599 --> 01:07:36,879
"All five positions: clear to engage!"

960
01:07:41,599 --> 01:07:43,559
"Two in position."

961
01:07:44,439 --> 01:07:46,399
"Decoy in sight."

962
01:07:46,559 --> 01:07:49,199
"Target at twelve o'clock.
Is that Frank Mendt?"

963
01:07:49,399 --> 01:07:51,359
Confirm, that's Frank Mendt.

964
01:07:53,959 --> 01:07:56,999
"Target carries in the
left hand a firearm."

965
01:07:57,199 --> 01:07:59,439
"Please confirm."
- "Yes, correct."

966
01:08:00,519 --> 01:08:03,239
"Could take him down for good."
- "Absolutely not!"

967
01:08:03,999 --> 01:08:06,639
Fire authorization is
given exclusively by me.

968
01:08:07,559 --> 01:08:09,519
"Understood."

969
01:08:12,039 --> 01:08:14,519
(Tense music)

970
01:08:24,399 --> 01:08:26,359
Meeting point.

971
01:08:26,599 --> 01:08:29,279
Is that Stefan Freund?
- Yes.

972
01:08:30,719 --> 01:08:33,079
I want to see now
my daughter.

973
01:08:45,239 --> 01:08:48,079
My wife is bringing you
your daughter now.

974
01:08:52,719 --> 01:08:54,679
(Cough)

975
01:08:54,879 --> 01:08:57,239
No! Wait!
That's not Stefan Freund.

976
01:08:57,399 --> 01:09:00,199
That's someone from the police.
I'm sorry.

977
01:09:01,599 --> 01:09:03,679
(Fast music)

978
01:09:05,839 --> 01:09:07,799
Please don't do that.

979
01:09:07,959 --> 01:09:11,599
(whispers:) We'll see each other
tonight. You bring me the right one.

980
01:09:11,799 --> 01:09:13,799
Of course.

981
01:09:14,999 --> 01:09:17,719
I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry!

982
01:09:18,879 --> 01:09:21,279
The man is free to leave.
No one follows.

983
01:09:21,439 --> 01:09:24,119
The man is clear to leave.
- (Screams:) Shit!

984
01:09:24,719 --> 01:09:26,679
Damn it!

985
01:09:31,359 --> 01:09:33,839
(Dark, pulsing music)

986
01:09:51,999 --> 01:09:54,039
That was an absolute shit plan.

987
01:09:54,199 --> 01:09:57,199
It wasn't a shit plan,
it just didn't work.

988
01:09:57,839 --> 01:10:00,319
If anything were to happen
to you, Thorsten,

989
01:10:00,479 --> 01:10:02,759
then we won't be
the elders anymore.

990
01:10:02,919 --> 01:10:04,999
We're not anymore.

991
01:10:12,559 --> 01:10:15,719
The biggest mistake was
trusting Thorsten.

992
01:10:16,559 --> 01:10:18,639
I don't know what to do anymore.

993
01:10:20,319 --> 01:10:22,519
(Soft music)

994
01:10:27,519 --> 01:10:29,639
I'll trade him for Maja.

995
01:10:30,399 --> 01:10:32,359
I'll do it.

996
01:10:33,599 --> 01:10:36,839
You get him out of prison
and put him in the car.

997
01:10:37,519 --> 01:10:39,479
That's all you have to do.

998
01:10:43,639 --> 01:10:46,519
We can't save them
both, it's not possible.

999
01:10:46,999 --> 01:10:50,799
So: put him in the car
and then walk away.

1000
01:10:53,519 --> 01:10:55,479
I'm not asking you for more.

1001
01:11:07,959 --> 01:11:09,919
(quietly:) Alright.

1002
01:11:13,959 --> 01:11:16,599
"We have the camper van.
It's parked in Filderstadt."

1003
01:11:17,119 --> 01:11:19,079
(Tense music)

1004
01:11:19,239 --> 01:11:21,559
Police, come in!
Hands on the table!

1005
01:11:21,719 --> 01:11:23,679
Sit over there!

1006
01:11:26,879 --> 01:11:29,629
Shit!
Lannert, Criminal Investigation, Stuttgart.

1007
01:11:29,655 --> 01:11:31,695
What's your license plate number?

1008
01:11:31,719 --> 01:11:34,399
What?
- What's your plate number?

1009
01:11:34,679 --> 01:11:37,279
SAB-124.

1010
01:11:37,479 --> 01:11:40,239
Shit! They swapped the plates!

1011
01:11:43,879 --> 01:11:46,039
(Dark music)

1012
01:11:50,799 --> 01:11:53,639
"NCK1 to Central."
- "Central, go ahead."

1013
01:11:53,799 --> 01:11:56,479
"The motorhome operation
in Filderstadt has failed."

1014
01:11:56,639 --> 01:11:58,999
"The suspects have
swapped their plates."

1015
01:11:59,159 --> 01:12:02,359
"Understood. Operation's over, all
units stand down."

1016
01:12:04,239 --> 01:12:06,399
 (Tense music)

1017
01:12:08,199 --> 01:12:10,159
See you shortly.

1018
01:12:36,839 --> 01:12:39,919
"Freund [Friend], that's a funny
name for a criminal, huh?"

1019
01:12:40,079 --> 01:12:42,039
Yeah.
- Right, Conni?

1020
01:12:50,159 --> 01:12:53,559
I don't have him on the list.
- He just came up.

1021
01:12:53,799 --> 01:12:55,759
For a lineup.

1022
01:12:55,999 --> 01:12:58,519
You could always call
the prosecutor's office.

1023
01:12:58,679 --> 01:13:02,172
Oh, come on! Please wait here.

1024
01:13:03,679 --> 01:13:06,039
(Suspenseful music)

1025
01:13:19,559 --> 01:13:21,599
We've already heard about it.

1026
01:13:21,799 --> 01:13:24,919
Any new leads?
- Plenty, especially about the Mendts.

1027
01:13:25,079 --> 01:13:27,039
But nothing recent about it.

1028
01:13:28,799 --> 01:13:30,759
A priest got in touch.

1029
01:13:30,919 --> 01:13:34,479
Mrs. Mendt lays flowers on her
daughter's grave every Tuesday.

1030
01:13:34,639 --> 01:13:36,599
Today is Thursday.

1031
01:13:37,339 --> 01:13:41,032
Yes ... Today is Thursday.

1032
01:13:43,719 --> 01:13:46,079
(Dark music)

1033
01:13:54,839 --> 01:13:56,799
I'm in a hurry.

1034
01:14:02,119 --> 01:14:04,079
Watch your head.

1035
01:14:20,159 --> 01:14:23,799
(Phone rings.)
(Alvarez:) This is Stammheim prison.

1036
01:14:24,319 --> 01:14:27,599
Do you know anything about a
confrontation with Mr. Freund?

1037
01:14:33,119 --> 01:14:36,279
Yes, I, um ... I had
forgotten, um ...

1038
01:14:36,519 --> 01:14:40,079
The cybercrime colleagues
wanted to borrow him,

1039
01:14:40,279 --> 01:14:43,119
because of the photos,
he has published online.

1040
01:14:43,599 --> 01:14:46,199
But we're in touch,
in case we need him.

1041
01:14:46,359 --> 01:14:48,319
Okay ...

1042
01:14:48,479 --> 01:14:50,439
Mr. Engel, can you hear me? Yes.

1043
01:14:50,599 --> 01:14:52,599
Yeah, that's fine.
Absolutely.

1044
01:14:52,759 --> 01:14:55,599
It was right,
that you pressed the issue. Thank you.

1045
01:14:55,759 --> 01:14:57,719
Speak later.

1046
01:15:13,159 --> 01:15:16,759
Go ahead and secure those things.
You know how it's done, right?

1047
01:15:21,479 --> 01:15:23,559
Who should the confrontation
be with?

1048
01:15:23,719 --> 01:15:26,079
That's the joke
about a confrontation,

1049
01:15:26,239 --> 01:15:28,199
that you don't know.

1050
01:15:28,359 --> 01:15:30,319
I'll be right back.

1051
01:15:47,599 --> 01:15:49,839
(Suspenseful music)

1052
01:15:54,759 --> 01:15:56,719
Where is Sebastian?

1053
01:15:58,239 --> 01:16:01,319
Umm, he wanted to stretch his
legs, have some time to himself.

1054
01:16:01,479 --> 01:16:04,359
Don't lie to me!
The taxi number is 216.

1055
01:16:04,519 --> 01:16:08,119
Should I ask dispatch
where they picked you up?

1056
01:16:08,279 --> 01:16:11,079
Or are you going to tell me that
that was at Stammheim prison?

1057
01:16:11,279 --> 01:16:13,599
You cooked this up together.
Where is he?

1058
01:16:13,879 --> 01:16:16,799
I don't know.
- He's heading in for his execution!

1059
01:16:18,319 --> 01:16:20,479
Where is Sebastian?

1060
01:16:20,639 --> 01:16:22,599
It's not about him, Thorsten.

1061
01:16:22,759 --> 01:16:25,519
It's not about Freund,
nor about me and you.

1062
01:16:25,679 --> 01:16:28,519
It's about Maja, nothing else.
- Yes, it is about Maja.

1063
01:16:28,679 --> 01:16:31,719
If I put a search out for Sebastian,
I won't find him.

1064
01:16:31,919 --> 01:16:34,359
But we can help
if we find Maja,

1065
01:16:34,599 --> 01:16:36,559
before he hands Freund over!
So.

1066
01:16:36,759 --> 01:16:39,999
Did he say anything?
A meeting with Mendt, for example?

1067
01:16:41,279 --> 01:16:43,239
No, he didn't.
- Damn it!

1068
01:16:45,159 --> 01:16:49,039
I'm asking because it's pretty much
certain Maja will be nearby.

1069
01:16:51,919 --> 01:16:54,199
They both want to kill themselves, right?

1070
01:16:55,199 --> 01:16:58,439
I would say goodbye to my daughter
beforehand.

1071
01:17:02,999 --> 01:17:04,959
(Cell phone rings.)

1072
01:17:06,559 --> 01:17:08,519
Yes?
- (Mendt:) "Do you have him?"

1073
01:17:11,439 --> 01:17:14,039
Yes.
- "Throw your phone away."

1074
01:17:14,359 --> 01:17:17,119
"Your new one is at the bus stop
Schlachthof."

1075
01:17:17,279 --> 01:17:19,639
"The phone is lying there in the trash can."

1076
01:17:19,999 --> 01:17:22,439
"Press speed dial key one."

1077
01:17:22,639 --> 01:17:24,599
Good.

1078
01:17:33,759 --> 01:17:35,719
Damn!

1079
01:17:35,959 --> 01:17:38,159
(Soft, melancholy music)

1080
01:18:08,119 --> 01:18:10,359
She probably won't be coming.

1081
01:18:10,599 --> 01:18:12,559
The flowers are fresh.

1082
01:18:14,839 --> 01:18:16,799
(He sighs.)

1083
01:18:18,759 --> 01:18:21,079
(Tense music)

1084
01:18:26,759 --> 01:18:28,719
If you had children ...

1085
01:18:30,839 --> 01:18:32,799
So?

1086
01:18:33,679 --> 01:18:36,039
Would you hand the man over then?

1087
01:18:44,279 --> 01:18:46,239
I would step aside.

1088
01:18:47,919 --> 01:18:49,879
Out?
- Of it.

1089
01:18:50,039 --> 01:18:51,999
Out of the whole thing.

1090
01:18:59,719 --> 01:19:02,039
(Gloomy music)

1091
01:19:24,119 --> 01:19:27,799
(Menadt:) "Bootz, you're driving to
the Stuttgart Locomotive Depot now."

1092
01:19:27,959 --> 01:19:31,039
"Keep your phone on,
put it in your jacket pocket."

1093
01:19:31,199 --> 01:19:33,279
"If you switch it
off, we're gone."

1094
01:19:33,479 --> 01:19:35,559
"Let us know,
when you're there."

1095
01:19:35,719 --> 01:19:37,679
Yes.

1096
01:19:41,359 --> 01:19:43,919
(Suspenseful music)

1097
01:19:58,199 --> 01:20:00,759
(A scream) Mrs.
Mendt, this is the police.

1098
01:20:00,919 --> 01:20:03,519
Where is the girl?
Where is Maja?

1099
01:20:03,679 --> 01:20:06,039
Tell us, where the girl is!

1100
01:20:06,199 --> 01:20:08,359
(She screams.)
Mrs. Mendt!

1101
01:20:08,679 --> 01:20:10,639
Mrs. Mendt!

1102
01:20:12,599 --> 01:20:14,599
Mrs. Mendt!

1103
01:20:15,039 --> 01:20:16,999
(shouting:) Mrs. Mendt!

1104
01:20:18,239 --> 01:20:20,559
You're a mother
too, just like me!

1105
01:20:20,759 --> 01:20:22,719
(She groans.)

1106
01:20:22,879 --> 01:20:24,839
Stay calm!

1107
01:20:27,519 --> 01:20:29,759
(quietly:) Yes ... Yes ...

1108
01:20:30,199 --> 01:20:32,159
Here.

1109
01:20:35,439 --> 01:20:38,519
That was my wife. And
that was Leni, my daughter.

1110
01:20:38,719 --> 01:20:41,719
At the hospital, they told me
both of them would survive!

1111
01:20:41,879 --> 01:20:45,039
They didn't make it. I
know what that means!

1112
01:20:45,199 --> 01:20:47,479
I know how it feels. Mrs. Mendt!

1113
01:20:47,639 --> 01:20:49,879
Tell us where Maja is! Please!

1114
01:20:50,359 --> 01:20:53,119
I know there's no
cure for the pain.

1115
01:20:53,279 --> 01:20:56,519
But I don't want my colleague
to go through the same thing.

1116
01:20:56,679 --> 01:20:59,199
Please tell us,
where the girl is.

1117
01:20:59,359 --> 01:21:01,319
Please!

1118
01:21:03,119 --> 01:21:05,079
Yes ...

1119
01:21:07,119 --> 01:21:09,079
Shit!

1120
01:21:09,759 --> 01:21:12,559
Ms. Mendt!
- Ms. Mendt! Shit!

1121
01:21:12,919 --> 01:21:14,879
(Ms. Mendt coughs and chokes.)

1122
01:21:15,679 --> 01:21:17,879
Ms. Mendt!
Oh God, shit!

1123
01:21:18,239 --> 01:21:20,199
(Gurgling)

1124
01:21:20,359 --> 01:21:22,319
Get the ambulance, now!

1125
01:21:22,479 --> 01:21:24,439
Ms. Mendt! Ms. Mendt!

1126
01:21:26,359 --> 01:21:29,039
Shit! Shit!

1127
01:21:34,999 --> 01:21:36,959
Ms. Mendt?

1128
01:21:38,079 --> 01:21:40,799
Nika! Nika, Nika, Nika!
- Can you hear me?

1129
01:21:41,599 --> 01:21:46,099
Nika, we need an emergency
location on number 0147-843231.

1130
01:21:48,759 --> 01:21:51,239
As fast as possible!
Hurry up!

1131
01:21:52,279 --> 01:21:54,599
(Suspenseful music)

1132
01:21:58,999 --> 01:22:01,079
"Yes?"
- I'm here.

1133
01:22:02,319 --> 01:22:05,639
Good. Can you see car
number three, the green one?

1134
01:22:06,159 --> 01:22:08,639
Green car ... Okay ...

1135
01:22:08,799 --> 01:22:10,759
"That's the frontmost car."

1136
01:22:11,159 --> 01:22:13,119
"
Ah, I can see it.

1137
01:22:13,279 --> 01:22:16,439
Good, step behind the car.
Now I can see you.

1138
01:22:16,599 --> 01:22:18,559
Come toward me.

1139
01:22:20,079 --> 01:22:22,679
(Suspenseful music)

1140
01:22:37,079 --> 01:22:39,039
Where is Freund?

1141
01:22:39,439 --> 01:22:41,399
In the car, in handcuffs.

1142
01:22:45,079 --> 01:22:47,359
Put down your service weapon,
slowly.

1143
01:22:47,519 --> 01:22:49,759
I ... I don't have a service weapon.

1144
01:22:50,439 --> 01:22:53,439
Mr. Mendt, I ...
I'm removing myself from the equation.

1145
01:22:53,679 --> 01:22:55,639
I can't give you Freund.

1146
01:22:55,799 --> 01:22:57,999
You'll have to
find someone else.

1147
01:22:59,359 --> 01:23:01,319
Then your daughter dies.

1148
01:23:02,639 --> 01:23:04,999
But not
because I won't give you someone,

1149
01:23:05,159 --> 01:23:07,119
but because you'll kill her.

1150
01:23:07,279 --> 01:23:10,519
It won't help you.
It won't bring you any closer to Freund.

1151
01:23:10,679 --> 01:23:13,199
You'll also have
killed a little girl.

1152
01:23:13,479 --> 01:23:15,679
Where is the car?
- The car? That ...

1153
01:23:18,359 --> 01:23:20,959
The car is in the yard
of a police station.

1154
01:23:21,119 --> 01:23:23,079
You're not getting to it.

1155
01:23:23,239 --> 01:23:25,879
I don't know what I should
do, do you understand?

1156
01:23:26,559 --> 01:23:30,039
I can't live with not saving my
daughter.

1157
01:23:30,199 --> 01:23:32,519
But I can't
be a friend to you either.

1158
01:23:32,679 --> 01:23:34,639
That can't be!

1159
01:23:34,799 --> 01:23:36,759
I'm sorry.

1160
01:23:37,759 --> 01:23:39,719
Can you help me?

1161
01:23:41,159 --> 01:23:43,439
(Tense music)

1162
01:23:46,279 --> 01:23:48,719
Please help me! Please!
- Yes, yes.

1163
01:23:55,759 --> 01:23:58,679
Show me,
how much you love your daughter.

1164
01:23:58,839 --> 01:24:00,799
What?

1165
01:24:03,799 --> 01:24:06,439
Your life
for your daughter's life.

1166
01:24:07,399 --> 01:24:09,479
(Driving music)

1167
01:24:10,599 --> 01:24:12,559
Show me.

1168
01:24:29,279 --> 01:24:31,599
(Suspenseful music)

1169
01:24:32,359 --> 01:24:34,319
I have your word?
- Yes!

1170
01:24:38,719 --> 01:24:40,679
(Clicking)

1171
01:24:51,799 --> 01:24:54,239
The RV is at the garden center.

1172
01:24:55,719 --> 01:24:57,839
East Business Park.

1173
01:24:59,959 --> 01:25:01,919
It's time now.

1174
01:25:04,199 --> 01:25:06,159
(Gunshot)

1175
01:25:09,679 --> 01:25:11,839
(Shrill whistle)

1176
01:25:15,159 --> 01:25:17,119
Oh God!

1177
01:25:24,079 --> 01:25:26,039
Oh God!

1178
01:25:29,359 --> 01:25:31,799
(Eerie music)

1179
01:25:35,079 --> 01:25:38,279
The RV is at the garden center
in the East Business District.

1180
01:25:45,679 --> 01:25:48,039
At the garden center in
the East Business District ...

1181
01:25:51,119 --> 01:25:53,799
(Eerie, atmospheric music)

1182
01:26:50,039 --> 01:26:51,999
How are you doing?

1183
01:26:53,119 --> 01:26:55,079
I'm fine.

1184
01:27:00,159 --> 01:27:03,039
I'm sorry for what I said
about your daughter.

1185
01:27:06,719 --> 01:27:09,079
(Eerie music)

1186
01:27:52,239 --> 01:27:54,239
SWR 2015

